{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams","id":963522,"title":"Why Silver Ladder should never fulfill their dreams","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-04T21:19:39-07:00","id":963522,"title":"Why Silver Ladder should never fulfill their dreams","content":"Simple clip from movie Absolutely Anything (2015) points that Seers of Throne can have right...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3L-62b8xlLk\" data-code=\"3L-62b8xlLk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3L-62b8xlLk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2016, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T21:30:04-07:00","id":963530,"title":"","content":"You need to fix the link.<br /> <br /> and while I'm usually down for knocking the Ladder down a peg or two, I am loaded with trepidation about an argument that validates the Seers. Just because I think most of us would be them doesn't mean I want to somehow make that more likely. We'll see what we have to actually say when we do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T22:14:42-07:00","id":963551,"title":"","content":"Fixed link<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3L-62b8xlLk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3L-62b8xlLk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3L-62b8xlLk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3L-62b8xlLk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T23:08:56-07:00","id":963566,"title":"","content":"Here's another take on the same idea, from The Matrix (1999).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RliCVnBXDi8\" data-code=\"RliCVnBXDi8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/RliCVnBXDi8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":".  adding in the movie title. 09-05-2016, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T01:19:50-07:00","id":963594,"title":"","content":"It says more about the Seer mindset than the Ladder I'd say. The mindset of that clip seems to be, that if you can't make the world perfect, then why bother?<br /> <br /> The Ladder aren't that stupid; they well know that their grand project takes a huge amount of work and effort. Plus they clearly do understand the idea of gradual improvement. You probably won't create a Utopia, but that's ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T02:28:57-07:00","id":963609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=963594#post963594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says more about the Seer mindset than the Ladder I'd say. The mindset of that clip seems to be, that if you can't make the world perfect, then why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather that every spell can have unforeseen consequences. Like saying goes: 'Hell is paved with good intentions.'<br /> <br /> Limited human minds cannot predict every possible results - it's also fundament of Wisdom-as-Trait.<br /> <br /> And that even Tearchs would overthrow Exarchs - What is certainty they will not become next Exarchs themselves?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T07:31:26-07:00","id":963686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=963609#post963609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather that every spell can have unforeseen consequences. Like saying goes: 'Hell is paved with good intentions.' Limited human minds cannot predict every possible results - it's also fundament of Wisdom-as-Trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? That's not exactly a new revelation. The SL have been at this for quite a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that even Tearchs would overthrow Exarchs - What is certainty they will not become next Exarchs themselves? </div> </div> </div>There isn't any; but that's a lame excuse not to help people. If you do nothing, you can be pretty certain the Exarchs aren't going anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:06:04-07:00","id":964300,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I also believe that Silver Ladder and Seers of the Throne have a lot in common.<br /> <br /> What if Seers were Silver Ladder Mages who, having a higher perspective, decided that the world would be better fallen and in Order than Ascended and in flux. I would like to portray them as harsh Keepers of Order rather than evil greedy sarumans. Maybe the Truth means terrible things for the Cosmos if every human could play with Nature's Laws.<br /> <br /> As George R. R. Martin puts it \u201cPeople often claim to hunger for truth, but seldom like the taste when it's served up.\u201d</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 09-06-2016, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:21:24-07:00","id":964368,"title":"","content":"I believe the official history of the Seers and the Ladder is that they were a single organization that split: They were the mages who went seeking after the hidden powers that had caused the Fall. They found the Exarchs.<br /> The Silver Ladder responded to the discovery of the tyrant kings of the Lie with defiance. The Seers of the Throne decided they would rather serve.<br /> I find it very strange how the Mage forums have an underlying current of 'let's see if we can justify the Seers of the Throne.' Their justification is the same many people in history and the present would give: Personal security and profit. Any corporation that uses child labor, any corrupt politician, any human trafficker: They justify themselves with self-interest. That's one major foundation of what the Seers are: Mages who chose self-interest and power over freedom and defiance. The Silver Ladder is still human - Thearchs have flaws, the organization has some ideas as a whole that I profoundly disagree with, but they do stand for human self-determination in the face of tyrant symbols of literal oppression.<br /> In short, the Ladder has ideals. It stands for a better world. One can disagree that the 'better world' of the Thearchs is better, in fact, but one can't argue they don't pursue a vision of utopia. Moreover, their utopia generally looks pretty good - it's a humanist one.<br /> The Seers stand for themselves and only themselves. Many individual Seers have ideals and justifications, but as an organization they are totally unprincipled. I mean, come on: They are literally a mystery cult that worships Oppression! They have faith in the power of xenophobia, violence, and surveillance to crush human aspiration, that is literally the cause they serve. An idealistic Seer is the most terrifying kind of mage - a self-interested one is far more comprehensible.<br /> The fact that the Seers are, in total, a minority of mages is a statement of faith in humanity that the game makes, and one I appreciate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:34:19-07:00","id":964377,"title":"","content":"The main reason that people feel a need to come up with more justification for the existence (via idealism or whatever) of the Seers is because they think selfishness is a flat motivator that can't do a perfectly good job of explaining a person's motives for doing evil. They think selfishness is too mustache twirling and cliche so they try to add more &quot;humanizing&quot; motivations. Personally, I'm fine with selfishness as a motivator, it's very, very human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:07:06-07:00","id":964404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964377#post964377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason that people feel a need to come up with more justification for the existence (via idealism or whatever) of the Seers is because they think selfishness is a flat motivator that can't do a perfectly good job of explaining a person's motives for doing evil. They think selfishness is too mustache twirling and cliche so they try to add more &quot;humanizing&quot; motivations. Personally, I'm fine with selfishness as a motivator, it's very, very human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, to me the Seers are ideologically boring, there is no way to work around that. They are the whole spectrum of the death eaters from harry potter from the coward-easily led of...the rat guy to the psycothic like the bellatrix. And there isnt much to the ideologically wise, whatever the draco-in-leather-pants trope wants to sell you on that one.<br /> <br /> However, like the death eaters they are interesting in their methodology from the profane urim to the ochemata.<br /> <br /> As for the silver ladder, problem with that video POV is that well, its human. If the exarch mold reality as they did them the idea that humans cant have everything they want because is agaisnt human nature, is a Lie (tm).<br /> <br /> So if the SL cast away the exarch and get rid of the Lie(tm) then what much of what we understand as human nature remains as it is?<br /> <br /> And this specific brand of navel gazing is why i run mage as &quot;Fireballs &amp; alleys&quot;, and lets the contemplation of reality to forums :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:37:57-07:00","id":964430,"title":"","content":"Ideally a game should be able to accomplish both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:55:34-07:00","id":964452,"title":"","content":"To me the Seers' theme has always been &quot;I got mine&quot;. Ranging from the guy who isn't going to stick his neck out for strangers that don't deserve it, to the apex predator, the guy who sees himself as a lion among sheep taking his due. They range from collaborators, to mafia made men and elitist celebrities who think they are above the common plebs. To me it always seemed like the various arguments about faith and the greater good belonged to Banishers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T13:37:13-07:00","id":964502,"title":"","content":"The Silver Ladder shouldnt' be in power because they would establish a thearchy where the Awakened basically rule the world unchallenged as an elite class, and everyone else would be second class. Well, other supernaturals might get a second class status, and mortals third class. Actually, not that different than right now, just with the people in charge different. That's a different hell-world than one created from careless wishes that result in war across the world and Sahara Desert living quarters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:09:21-07:00","id":964505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964377#post964377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason that people feel a need to come up with more justification for the existence (via idealism or whatever) of the Seers is because they think selfishness is a flat motivator that can't do a perfectly good job of explaining a person's motives for doing evil. They think selfishness is too mustache twirling and cliche so they try to add more &quot;humanizing&quot; motivations. Personally, I'm fine with selfishness as a motivator, it's very, very human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with you if it weren't for the fact that the book flat-out says that all seers know the Exarchs are evil and serve them anyway. Cults don't work that way. Cultists convince themselves that they are the good guys, that their leader is perfect, and condemn all evidence to the contrary as heresy. It's all about isolating yourself from dissenting opinions so you can convince yourself that you are part of a utopia.<br /> <br /> Someone who joins the Seers out of selfishness or fear is not going to just become a sociopath because the Seers tell him to. He'll either have a nervous breakdown, or will rationalize everything he's doing as being necessary for the greater good. This is where the complaints about the Seers are coming from. People don't consciously accept that they're evil because they're greedy. They block out all evidence that they're evil, condemn everyone outside of their group as corrupt, and convince themselves that their greed is part of a holy purpose. They do everything they can do to protect their self-perception as a good person. That is not consistent with the book's portrayal of the Seers. Take this quote for example:<br /> <br /> &quot;I have spent the best years of my life giving people the lighter pleasures, helping them have a good time, and all I get is abuse, the existence of a hunted man.&quot;<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Capone\" target=\"_blank\">Al Capone</a><br /> <br /> Al Capone, a vicious gangster, convinced himself that he was a public benefactor - a person working for the greater good. THIS is how the Seers should see themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 09-06-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:11:26-07:00","id":964509,"title":"","content":"@MCN<br /> <br /> The difference is that Thearchs want people to constantly strive to move up the Ladder, and want to help them in that effort. Hence the order's name.<br /> <br /> A Seer wants to go up by stepping on everyone else and actively strives to keep the others down.<br /> <br /> It's not as much about hierarchy itself, it's about forces moving humanity collectively up that hierarchy versus forces trying to keep it under the cosmic tyrant's heels, forever in misery and without hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-06-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:15:08-07:00","id":964514,"title":"","content":"Technically speaking, if the Silver Ladder got their way completely and totally, notwithstanding any magical or social complications...<br /> <br /> Anyone who desires Awakening would Awaken. Anyone who didn't have that kind of obsessive magical drive would not be in charge of running reality but would be a citizen - the Ladder and the Free Council are tied for 'most gung-ho about humanity.' All the spirits, the other supernatural splats... well, they're gonna be down and out in Hieraconis, because the Silver Ladder explicitly and ONLY cares about humanity. Vampires would be extinct, werewolves would be employed as enforcers and proxy rulers of the Shadow's spirits at best, and so on. Changelings might get help from the Ladder on the grounds that they are human victims of an outside force, I suppose.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder is not, in fact, anti-Sleeper. They just think only the Wise know enough about the universe to make the right decisions - they are quite explicitly interested in building an esoteric variation on Plato's Republic. It's not a democracy, but it is intended to be a well-run society in which humanity rules in splendor over the world. An attractive proposition! Also a wildly hubristic one, since they're not just explicitly utopian, they admit that the current laws of reality don't support the creation of their utopia, which is why the laws must be changed.<br /> <br /> You can't fault them for idealism. You can fault them for pragmatism, and for the classic 'well if we had a perfectly just ruler, why would we need elections?' rhetoric. They are not, in fact, angling to be tin-pot tyrants, any more than the Free Council is advocating for total stateless anarchy.<br /> <br /> Of course, they're a long, long way from any of this coming to fruition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:18:43-07:00","id":964518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964505#post964505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree with you if it weren't for the fact that the book flat-out says that all seers know the Exarchs are evil and serve them anyway. Cults don't work that way. Cultists convince themselves that they are the good guys, that their leader is perfect, and condemn all evidence to the contrary as heresy. It's all about isolating yourself from dissenting opinions so you can convince yourself that you are part of a utopia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how most of the discussion has struck me - it's seemed to mostly focus on making the Seers somewhat justified, rather than explaining how they can convince themselves that the Lie is, in fact, just fine. The Seers of the Throne book was pretty clear that Seers are often convinced of various things, many of which are 'I'm just doing my job' or 'if it wasn't me it would be somebody else' or 'people are evil and deserve this.' Seers maintain the Lie, and that includes lying to themselves, I thought that was pretty explicit in the order writeup in both editions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:29:08-07:00","id":964528,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> I didn't say they don't justify it to themselves, I said that accepting that underneath any pretense they build for themselves having them be played straight as selfish bastards isn't a problem to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:29:33-07:00","id":964529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfSilkAndStone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964518#post964518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how most of the discussion has struck me - it's seemed to mostly focus on making the Seers somewhat justified, rather than explaining how they can convince themselves that the Lie is, in fact, just fine. The Seers of the Throne book was pretty clear that Seers are often convinced of various things, many of which are 'I'm just doing my job' or 'if it wasn't me it would be somebody else' or 'people are evil and deserve this.' Seers maintain the Lie, and that includes lying to themselves, I thought that was pretty explicit in the order writeup in both editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2e core book contradicts what you're saying.<br /> <br /> &quot;No mage serves the Throne out of altruism. Even the deluded or willfully ignorant find themselves quickly disabused of notions of fighting the good fight.&quot; - p.54<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964528#post964528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> I didn't say they don't justify it to themselves, I said that accepting that underneath any pretense they build for themselves having them be played straight as selfish bastards isn't a problem to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with there being Seers who are simply greedy, but the book says that NO seer works under any altruistic pretense, which I don't agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 09-06-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:51:56-07:00","id":964545,"title":"","content":"@Prometheus<br /> Ummm.... I wasn't comparing Ladder and Seers? I was saying that the video had nothing to do with the Ladder's vision. You must have me mistaken with others. Frankly, I'm sick to death of the Seer discussions. Don't care. Everyone run the bloody villains however you want.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3547\" data-vbnamecard=\"3547\">SonOfSilkAndStone</a> <br /> No one said the Ladder were &quot;anti-Sleeper.&quot; The Mysterium are anti-Sleeper. However, it remains a fact that the Ladder supports a hierarchy with the Awakened on top ruling over all other people, irregardless of actual ability to put their magic to practice, morals, or inclination. They also claim that unAwakened humans, even if its being a non-mage by choice, should be led by the Awakened, with no say in the matter.<br /> <br /> That is simple, unescapable classism built into the very nature of the Silver Ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:39:09-07:00","id":964665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964505#post964505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree with you if it weren't for the fact that the book flat-out says that all seers know the Exarchs are evil and serve them anyway. Someone who joins the Seers out of selfishness or fear is not going to just become a sociopath because the Seers tell him to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with you. In the same paragraph you quote on page 54, it says that Seers do what they are told. <b>Seers of the Throne follow their orders</b> and they profit from it. They are lavishly rewarded for their obedience and, to quote <i>Star Trek: TNG,</i> &quot;The Most Toys,&quot; punishments can be <i>equally lavish.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He'll either have a nervous breakdown, or will rationalize everything he's doing as being necessary for the greater good. </div> </div> </div>Right. The same paragraph on page 54, which you quote from, says as much. The exact word they use is &quot;traumatic.&quot; It is extremely traumatic being a Seer of the Throne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is where the complaints about the Seers are coming from. People don't consciously accept that they're evil because they're greedy. </div> </div> </div>They consciously accept that they are evil because they believe they will get away with it. Who's to stop them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They block out all evidence that they're evil, condemn everyone outside of their group as corrupt, and convince themselves that their greed is part of a holy purpose. They do everything they can do to protect their self-perception as a good person. That is not consistent with the book's portrayal of the Seers. Take this quote for example:<br /> <br /> &quot;I have spent the best years of my life giving people the lighter pleasures, helping them have a good time, and all I get is abuse, the existence of a hunted man.&quot;<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Capone\" target=\"_blank\">Al Capone</a><br /> <br /> Al Capone, a vicious gangster, convinced himself that he was a public benefactor - a person working for the greater good. THIS is how the Seers should see themselves. </div> </div> </div>Do you think Al Capone believed he was a public benefactor when he was murdering people? Or do you think he was protecting his business? His profits. I don't think he murdered people because he was a psychopath. I think he murdered people because he was greedy. The same as drug cartels and white slavery rings. And the people who work for those Kingpins? Do you think they to what they are told because they believe they are doing something good? Or do you think they do what they are told because they will be rewarded handsomely and disobedience means brutal punishment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:01:24-07:00","id":964683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964665#post964665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Right. The same paragraph on page 54, which you quote from, says as much. The exact word they use is &quot;traumatic.&quot; It is extremely traumatic being a Seer of the Throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but living that way is not sustainable. Unless you start rationalizing your moral conflicts away, you'll soon wind up an invalid.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964665#post964665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They consciously accept that they are evil because they believe they will get away with it. Who's to stop them?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't consciously accept that they're evil at all in the first place.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964665#post964665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Do you think Al Capone believed he was a public benefactor when he was murdering people? Or do you think he was protecting his business? His profits. I don't think he murdered people because he was a psychopath. I think he murdered people because he was greedy. The same as drug cartels and white slavery rings. And the people who work for those Kingpins? Do you think they to what they are told because they believe they are doing something good? Or do you think they do what they are told because they will be rewarded handsomely and disobedience means brutal punishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I absolutely do think Capone considered himself a public benefactor when he was murdering people. That's my point. He may have had other motives as well, but he rationalized and justified them as being in service of a greater mission, and instead blamed the evil on his enemies.<br /> <br /> That's why I don't like it when the book says Seers can't be deluded enough to think that they're the good guys. That level of delusion is precisely how cults work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 09-06-2016, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:15:59-07:00","id":964691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964683#post964683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but living that way is not sustainable. Unless you start rationalizing your moral conflicts away, you'll soon wind up an invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. There are plenty of traumatized people who live out their lives perfectly fine. That's the problem with trauma, it's largely invisible, and can be kept secret. A perfectly reasonable means of rationalizing away your moral conflicts is to say, &quot;If I don't do this -- they'll kill me...or worse.&quot; It's not a good lifestyle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, they don't consciously accept that they're evil at all in the first place. </div> </div> </div>When they do harmful things to others, simply because they are commanded to do so, what do you think they are saying to themselves? How might someone become disabused of the notion that they are working for the greater good?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes I absolutely do think Capone considered himself a public benefactor when he was murdering people. That's my point. He may have had other motives as well, but he rationalized and justified them as being in service of a greater mission, and instead blamed the evil on his enemies. </div> </div> </div>People who believe they are in service of a greater mission don't do the things Al Capone did. They don't do the things drug cartels and sex slavers do. I think when Al Capone said that, he was lying and he knew it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I don't like it when the book says Seers can't be deluded enough to think that they're the good guys. That level of delusion is precisely how cults work. </div> </div> </div>If you don't like it, that's fine. But don't say that book supports your view, which is how you entered this discussion, and that's the actual thing we're talking about.<br /> <br /> Seers are selfish. Maybe they like money or fame or power or sex or drugs or you name it. Maybe they just like to keep breathing. Their motivation is to be rewarded or their obedience and to avoid being punished for disobedience. They are Skinner's behaviorists utopia! And there's nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> Other Orders don't think that's the best way to live your life and use your magic. And there's nothing wrong with that either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:28:51-07:00","id":964695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964545#post964545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is simple, unescapable classism built into the very nature of the Silver Ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I entirely disagree with you, but usually in a classist society those at the top intend to keep it that way instead of hoping that everyone can get to the level of privilege that they currently enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:44:47-07:00","id":964700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964691#post964691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. There are plenty of traumatized people who live out their lives perfectly fine. That's the problem with trauma, it's largely invisible, and can be kept secret. A perfectly reasonable means of rationalizing away your moral conflicts is to say, &quot;If I don't do this -- they'll kill me...or worse.&quot; It's not a good lifestyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do those people constantly confront the object of their trauma on a day to day basis without somehow denying it, rationalizing it, or somehow deluding themselves into thinking it's ok?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When they do harmful things to others, simply because they are commanded to do so, what do you think they are saying to themselves? How might someone become disabused of the notion that they are working for the greater good? </div> </div> </div>My orders came from the gods of this world, and it's only through their grace that mankind exists at all. The world is obviously as perfect as it can be, or they wouldn't have made it this way. Therefore it's my duty to serve them to prevent all the other worse worlds that would arise if their power were to ever wane.<br /> <br /> If they want me to kill this person, then that person obviously deserves it. They must have some secret sin that's unknown to me. Or maybe they're fated to destroy the world, and this is the only option. Or maybe it's just that mankind in general is fundamentally evil - excluding the Seers of course, who have transcended such flaws. These brutish ravenous sleepers continually refused to obey the Exarchs' perfect plan, and sadly left the Exarchs no choice but to cage them up for their own good and for the good of all creation. Regardless, these orders were handed down from the Exarchs, and the Exarchs are infallible, so whatever the reason, it's justified. I don't need to think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964691#post964691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who believe they are in service of a greater mission don't do the things Al Capone did. They don't do the things drug cartels and sex slavers do. I think when Al Capone said that, he was lying and he knew it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they do those things. One of the fundamental aspects of a cult is that its members want to do good. They delude themselves into thinking that their leader and their mission are infallible, and eventually they're justifying almost anything, including murder. It just takes extra effort and mental gymnastics to justify it. You convince yourself that your goal is noble and holy, that the ends justify the means, and that everyone outside your in-group is corrupt and working to destroy the world, so it doesn't matter if they get hurt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't like it, that's fine. But don't say that book supports your view, which is how you entered this discussion, and that's the actual thing we're talking about.<br /> <br /> Seers are selfish. Maybe they like money or fame or power or sex or drugs or you name it. Maybe they just like to keep breathing. Their motivation is to be rewarded or their obedience and to avoid being punished for disobedience. They are Skinner's behaviorists utopia! And there's nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> Other Orders don't think that's the best way to live your life and use your magic. And there's nothing wrong with that either. </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the book supports my view. I'm saying the 2e corebook contradicts my view, and contradicts previous books on the Seers, and that's why I have a problem with the corebook's presentation of Seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 09-06-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:51:36-07:00","id":964704,"title":"","content":"I mean to ask: When someone knows they are not working for the greater good, they they are oppressive tyrants because that's how they roll, what do they tell themselves?<br /> <br /> That's the Seers of the Throne. They might have gone into it with altruistic motives, but then are quickly disabused of that notion. How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:00:55-07:00","id":964708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964704#post964704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean to ask: When someone knows they are not working for the greater good, they they are oppressive tyrants because that's how they roll, what do they tell themselves?<br /> <br /> That's the Seers of the Throne. They might have gone into it with altruistic motives, but then are quickly disabused of that notion. How?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's not just 'how they roll.' It's also 'how the world rolls,' as the world is controlled by the Exarchs and coming face-to-face with them is a very powerful way of getting that across. For the Seers, the idea of devoting your life to resisting them 'for the greater good,' as if there is one, is an objective and self-indulgent waste of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-06-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:02:33-07:00","id":964711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964704#post964704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean to ask: When someone knows they are not working for the greater good, they they are oppressive tyrants because that's how they roll, what do they tell themselves?<br /> <br /> That's the Seers of the Throne. They might have gone into it with altruistic motives, but then are quickly disabused of that notion. How?</div> </div> </div> </div>My answer is that in many cases they are not disabused of that notion. They simply delude themselves further and further and further, inventing justifications and hiding from or condemning dissenting opinions as heresy. Simply put, no one thinks they're a bad person, no matter how bad they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T20:07:53-07:00","id":964738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964502#post964502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Ladder shouldnt' be in power because they would establish a thearchy where the Awakened basically rule the world unchallenged as an elite class, and everyone else would be second class. Well, other supernaturals might get a second class status, and mortals third class. Actually, not that different than right now, just with the people in charge different. That's a different hell-world than one created from careless wishes that result in war across the world and Sahara Desert living quarters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much, This.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T20:58:30-07:00","id":964752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964502#post964502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Ladder shouldnt' be in power because they would establish a thearchy where the Awakened basically rule the world unchallenged as an elite class, and everyone else would be second class. Well, other supernaturals might get a second class status, and mortals third class. Actually, not that different than right now, just with the people in charge different. That's a different hell-world than one created from careless wishes that result in war across the world and Sahara Desert living quarters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think the Silver Ladders would put mages 1st, humans 2nd and other supernaturals as 3rd. Vampires permanently prevent a soul from awakening when they give the embrace, werewolves spread non-awakening genetics through mankind, the gentry make changelings who can't awaken. Every other supernatural represents a human who should have awakened but now never can, tends to create a bit of prejudice for the Thearchs.<br /> <br /> Spoiler warning coming for the TV show the 4400 if you haven't watched it yet. In the 4400 they explore the alternative well. One of the characters fears the growing gap between the wealthy and the poor, so they're giving this magic super-drug to everyone that can give you magical powers. However 50% of people's brains can't handle the drug and they die as soon as they take it. The guy still wants everyone on Earth to take the drug because they think that a future without division is worth 3.5 billion deaths, and otherwise you'll have a divided society between those with powers and those without. As they put it one generation of sacrifice is worth it to save the future.<br /> <br /> So just think, the plan could be a whole lot scarier.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:07:58-07:00","id":964755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964711#post964711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My answer is that in many cases they are not disabused of that notion. They simply delude themselves further and further and further, inventing justifications and hiding from or condemning dissenting opinions as heresy. Simply put, no one thinks they're a bad person, no matter how bad they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think it's impossible for someone to know and understand they live in a culture of oppression and tyranny and then ingratiate themselves into that culture because the alternative is hazardous to one's survival?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:21:30-07:00","id":964760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964752#post964752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewolves spread non-awakening genetics through mankind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually nothing keeps wolf-blooded from Awakening except the First Change, and neither of them are exactly determined by genetics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every other supernatural represents a human who should have awakened but now never can, tends to create a bit of prejudice for the Thearchs. </div> </div> </div>I believe a Promethean who has become human can Awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:23:14-07:00","id":964762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964755#post964755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think it's impossible for someone to know and understand they live in a culture of oppression and tyranny and then ingratiate themselves into that culture because the alternative is hazardous to one's survival?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strangely enough, yes. I realize that it's counter-intuitive but the human brain basically doesn't work that way for at least the vast majority of humans. There is some very interesting psychological research on this topic about development in oppressive regimes or around state sponsored atrocities. It has a huge impact on people.<br /> <br /> Basically put we're social animals, we want to be similar to the people around us and it causes us distress to deviate from it. While we can be selective to some extent with where we identify and with whom, we really need to be associated with other people who share our value system. Long term cognitive dissonance, holding one value publicly and another privately is extraordinarily damaging to the human psyche. It's why undercover work is such an extraordinary task for the police and tends to result in a LOT of therapy being needed afterwards.<br /> <br /> With the exception of those people suffering a few rare mental disorders, humans need to believe that what they're doing is right even if forced to do so by outside compulsion. Gradually we tend to internalize a belief system that justifies our actions, at least eventually and if deprived of alternatives and coping mechanisms.<br /> <br /> Although Mages may not function the same way as they possess Gnosis and Wisdom, thus they cannot suffer breaking points. So... um, I'm not sure how it would work for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:24:18-07:00","id":964763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964755#post964755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You think it's impossible for someone to know and understand they live in a culture of oppression and tyranny and then ingratiate themselves into that culture because the alternative is hazardous to one's survival?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No. I just think that they do that by deluding themselves to one degree or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:38:18-07:00","id":964773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964760#post964760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually nothing keeps wolf-blooded from Awakening except the First Change, and neither of them are exactly determined by genetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, although I was using genetics as short-hand for heredity. It may not be in their DNA specifically but werewolves are werewolves because they have werewolf ancestors. Something like one in four wolf-blooded are going to experience the First Change (at least in Blood of the Wolf, not sure if this is still true). Also from an awakening standpoint wolf-blooded are basically somewhere between Sleepwalkers and Proximi, both of which are useful but considered less likely to awaken according to pentacle orthodoxy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe a Promethean who has become human can Awaken. </div> </div> </div>I don't see any reason why not.They're human now, they just took the long way of getting there. Likewise a resurrected sleeper could probably awaken or other extraordinary ways of becoming a human in Chronicles. However they're pretty rare so it's rather a fringe case. Plus Prometheans have their own reasons they'd often be treated as second class citizens or worse thanks to the disquiet. <br /> <br /> However I imagine the orthodox Thearch answer would be that the creation of Prometheans is an act of Hubris, but that they should be helped on their pilgrimage in order to add one more potential awakened soul to the population.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:59:19-07:00","id":964787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964773#post964773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may not be in their DNA specifically but werewolves are werewolves because they have werewolf ancestors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, no. Or at least, if they are, it's the same way that 'all people are from Africa,' because werewolves have been interbreeding with humanity for more than seven thousand years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also from an awakening standpoint wolf-blooded are basically somewhere between Sleepwalkers and Proximi, both of which are useful but considered less likely to awaken according to pentacle orthodoxy. </div> </div> </div>Have to take your word for that, there's nothing about it in the books. Though some of them think lycanthropy is spread by bite and werewolves don't eat people so they're not exactly scoring 100 on their true and false tests.<br /> <br /> It's worth keeping in mind that the Silver Ladder don't seem entirely gung-ho about humanity. 'Humanity is magical' is the domain of the Free Council. The Silver Ladder is more concerned with proximi and Sleepwalkers, with Sleepers as a whole being something that must be dealt with, ideally through some sort of illumination. But it seems like if they could guarantee a sizable enough populace of Sleepwalkers that would then be <i>guaranteed </i>to give birth to further Sleepwalkers, and so on down the line, the extermination of the Sleepers holding them back might be an option placed on the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T22:26:27-07:00","id":964792,"title":"","content":"Something to remember is that the Silver Ladder's goal isn't just the death of the Lie; the death of the Lie is a <i>means to an end</i>. The goal is for every soul to <i>Awaken</i>, and possibly to eventually Ascend. A theocracy where power is confined to the hands of a few is either a transitional state or a <i>failure</i> state.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder is the Path to Victory. It's not victory until all are Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T22:38:44-07:00","id":964796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964792#post964792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to remember is that the Silver Ladder's goal isn't just the death of the Lie; the death of the Lie is a <i>means to an end</i>. The goal is for every soul to <i>Awaken</i>, and possibly to eventually Ascend. A theocracy where power is confined to the hands of a few is either a transitional state or a <i>failure</i> state.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder is the Path to Victory. It's not victory until all are Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it about everyone Awakening? I never read the Order book, just going by the second edition core, but it says in the Ladder section, under Victory, 'the Ladder believes that everyone and anyone deserves the right to move to a rung that best suits her, even if it's not at the top. Let artists be artists, let managers, manage...and let mages work miracles. Awakened souls have a destiny and an obligation to uplift the Sleepers and bring Sleepwalkers to Awakening.'<br /> <br /> Are you saying that that's a two step ladder, all Sleepers to Sleepwalkers, then all <i>those </i>Sleepwalkers to Awakening? I suppose three, if Ascension's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T22:48:30-07:00","id":964798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=963530#post963530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to fix the link.<br /> <br /> and while I'm usually down for knocking the Ladder down a peg or two, I am loaded with trepidation about an argument that validates the Seers. Just because I think most of us would be them doesn't mean I want to somehow make that more likely. We'll see what we have to actually say when we do.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't even be slightly tempted to be a Seer. Government work is the devil. Why be a flunky when you can be a king?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T22:51:05-07:00","id":964800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964798#post964798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't even be slightly tempted to be a Seer. Government work is the devil. Why be a flunky when you can be a king?</div> </div> </div> </div>Be wary of your nevers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T23:02:20-07:00","id":964804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964529#post964529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2e core book contradicts what you're saying.<br /> <br /> &quot;No mage serves the Throne out of altruism. Even the deluded or willfully ignorant find themselves quickly disabused of notions of fighting the good fight.&quot; - p.54<br /> <br /> <br /> I can agree with there being Seers who are simply greedy, but the book says that NO seer works under any altruistic pretense, which I don't agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div> Disagree all you want but it's clear you're wrong.\u200b Greed is just the beginning of their failure state that they 100% support once they achieve the status to receive preaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T23:11:05-07:00","id":964812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964800#post964800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be wary of your nevers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Money is nice but it's such a simple thing to if you're a mage. I'm a big believer in the saying &quot;A man must know his limitations&quot;. And the path &quot;Good intentions leads straight to Hell&quot;. The path &quot;real good and true wisdom&quot; is crooked and a path far less traveled. So no the path the Seers offer isn't the least bit tempting to me.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T23:14:09-07:00","id":964817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964812#post964812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Money is nice but it's such a simple thing to if you're a mage. I'm a big believer in the saying &quot;A man must know his limitations&quot;. And the path &quot;Good intentions leads straight to Hell&quot;. The path &quot;real good and true wisdom&quot; is crooked and a path far less traveled. So no the path the Seers offer isn't the least bit tempting to me.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Think less money, more &quot;Gee, the mysteries of the universe are hard, and my obsessions could ruin my life. if only there was some force in the universe that could shortcut revelation for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The high life is a perk. The real prize is giving up and letting the gods reveal the Truth to you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah, actually noted-somehow I only read the first half.<br /> <br /> All the same, be wary of your nevers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T23:39:01-07:00","id":964821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964773#post964773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true, although I was using genetics as short-hand for heredity. It may not be in their DNA specifically but werewolves are werewolves because they have werewolf ancestors. Something like one in four wolf-blooded are going to experience the First Change (at least in Blood of the Wolf, not sure if this is still true). Also from an awakening standpoint wolf-blooded are basically somewhere between Sleepwalkers and Proximi, both of which are useful but considered less likely to awaken according to pentacle orthodoxy. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see any reason why not.They're human now, they just took the long way of getting there. Likewise a resurrected sleeper could probably awaken or other extraordinary ways of becoming a human in Chronicles. However they're pretty rare so it's rather a fringe case. Plus Prometheans have their own reasons they'd often be treated as second class citizens or worse thanks to the disquiet. <br /> <br /> However I imagine the orthodox Thearch answer would be that the creation of Prometheans is an act of Hubris, but that they should be helped on their pilgrimage in order to add one more potential awakened soul to the population.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Proximi are more likely to Awaken than Sleepers, not less.<br /> <br /> As to the thread: The Ladder do have a model for society that includes more tiers than just &quot;Sleeper or Mage&quot;: it's a <i>Ladder</i>, not a step. If it's a binary &quot;mages are better than Sleepers, and we will keep everyone where theynare&quot; you're after, look to the Seers.<br /> <br /> Seers backstab one another and paranoicly watch out for their lessers while plotting against their superiors in the Pyramid. which is so full of obtuse titles it's hard to know where you are.<br /> <br /> The Ladder break their vision of society down into several broad roles which they help people find their most fulfilling place within: they don't want everyone to Awaken, they want everyone whose nature calls to being a mage to Awaken, which is a big difference.<br /> <br /> The Ladder do things like supporting artists being artists rather than wasting their talent as managers. And also helping efective managers who find their fulfilment in it become trusted managers rather than wasting time on the novel society tells them to write. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Seers make sure artists starve, because fuck anyone who isn't a Seer.<br /> <br /> Dig?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T23:41:28-07:00","id":964824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964817#post964817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think less money, more &quot;Gee, the mysteries of the universe are hard, and my obsessions could ruin my life. if only there was some force in the universe that could shortcut revelation for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The high life is a perk. The real prize is giving up and letting the gods reveal the Truth to you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah, actually noted-somehow I only read the first half.<br /> <br /> All the same, be wary of your nevers.</div> </div> </div> </div> I \u200bget you but I'm thinking you don't understand my IRL mindset and what I would do if I actually were a mage and presented with the six choices. I believe anything good in life requires hard work and I my standards for myself are brutal. Hence I totally get and love the Silver Ladder and are disgusted by the Seers of the Throne. It isn't even a question to me. The Ladder uplifts and encourages everyone to be their best version of themselves. The Seers purposely keep you down because they don't want the competition. Greed, Envy, Jealousy and Sloth are typical Seer qualities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T23:53:39-07:00","id":964827,"title":"","content":"For reference, the Silver Ladder of Being:<br /> <br /> Oracles<br /> Archmasters<br /> Awakened Mages<br /> Those who guide other Sleepers : Philosophers and Priests<br /> Experts in a subject: historians, scientists, IT architects, etc<br /> Those who direct others: Managers, Politicians, businesspeople<br /> Those who use violence and threats to keep order: Police, mobsters, soldiers<br /> Those who are famous: movie stars, solcialites, megastar musicians<br /> Everyone else<br /> Supernatural beings other than mages.<br /> <br /> That's right! among other amusing things: <br /> <br /> A thearch has greater respect for a mob hitman than for someone famous for just being famous, and for the most struggling homeless person than for a Changeling.<br /> <br /> ultimately, they just want all humans to become the thing they're good at and happy doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T00:09:37-07:00","id":964829,"title":"","content":"It's why the Free Council scares me. They believe in actual democracy and believe EVERYONE should be in the club. Not even my Nation the USA is that insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T00:41:45-07:00","id":964833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964829#post964829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even my Nation the USA is that insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the FC refers to 'Democracy', it's a value being contrasted with 'Hierarchy'. It's not democracy as in the style of government (though it can include that). By the FC standards, the USA is incredibly hierarchical; any nation-state is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T00:56:53-07:00","id":964837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964833#post964833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the FC refers to 'Democracy', it's a value being contrasted with 'Hierarchy'. It's not democracy as in the style of government (though it can include that). By the FC standards, the USA is incredibly hierarchical; any nation-state is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... yeah. The FC's tenets, interpreted in the modern senses, are anarchistic. That really underscores the point Kumiko just made.<br /> <br /> Using a more classical interpretation, they include things like republics and gothar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T00:59:33-07:00","id":964838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964821#post964821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Proximi are more likely to Awaken than Sleepers, not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thankyou, I clearly had it around the wrong way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:22:16-07:00","id":964848,"title":"","content":"As to why certain types of people are on higher or lower rungs of the Ladder, according to orthodox thearchs:<br /> <br /> It's about the responsibility of the enlightened to give guidance to those less enlightened. That's why it goes mage-priest-technocrat-manager-bully-famous-follower-monster.<br /> <br /> Clavigers tell student thearchs not to apply these classifications on face value (is a musician influential because she's a truly excellent composer-songwriter, or because she win pop idol? Is a businessman an actual good manager dedicated to his employee's interests, or a bullying blowhard? Is a priest just mouthing doctrine, or does she genuinely tens to spiritual needs of her followers?)<br /> <br /> And they're especially not supposed to judge other mages by these standards. Although they totally do, leading to things like the stereotypically one-sided relationships between Ladder, Council, and Arrow. Common wisdom is that the Ladder have more regard for libertines than Arrows because of where they would fall on the Ladder if they were Sleepers, despite the Arrow liking them way more back than the Libertines do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:27:14-07:00","id":964850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964827#post964827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference, the Silver Ladder of Being:<br /> <br /> Oracles<br /> Archmasters<br /> Awakened Mages<br /> Those who guide other Sleepers : Philosophers and Priests<br /> Experts in a subject: historians, scientists, IT architects, etc<br /> Those who direct others: Managers, Politicians, businesspeople<br /> Those who use violence and threats to keep order: Police, mobsters, soldiers<br /> Those who are famous: movie stars, solcialites, megastar musicians<br /> Everyone else<br /> Supernatural beings other than mages.<br /> <br /> That's right! among other amusing things:<br /> <br /> A thearch has greater respect for a mob hitman than for someone famous for just being famous, and for the most struggling homeless person than for a Changeling.<br /> <br /> ultimately, they just want all humans to become the thing they're good at and happy doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice the higher levels use wisdom and knowledge while the lower rungs use advantage and violence more and more? Movie stars are usually just people in the right place at the right time and have no skill at leadership. Mobsters and the like are leaders and learned to be so despite being selfish and evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-07-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:38:59-07:00","id":964854,"title":"","content":"But it isn't black and white. The Silver Ladder respects leaders and teachers more than pure position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T03:28:19-07:00","id":964877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]For reference, the Silver Ladder of Being:<br /> <br /> Oracles<br /> Archmasters<br /> Awakened Mages<br /> Those who guide other Sleepers : Philosophers and Priests<br /> Experts in a subject: historians, scientists, IT architects, etc<br /> Those who direct others: Managers, Politicians, businesspeople<br /> Those who use violence and threats to keep order: Police, mobsters, soldiers<br /> Those who are famous: movie stars, solcialites, megastar musicians<br /> Everyone else<br /> Supernatural beings other than mages.<br /> <br /> That's right! among other amusing things: <br /> <br /> A thearch has greater respect for a mob hitman than for someone famous for just being famous, and for the most struggling homeless person than for a Changeling.<br /> <br /> ultimately, they just want all humans to become the thing they're good at and happy doing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Holy @#$#@. I take back everything I ever said. The implications of the Silver Ladder ideal is even worse than I ever imagined. Dear Goddess, the Ladder are officially some of the scariest people in the CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T04:47:43-07:00","id":964894,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the constant presence of rainbows and unicorns enough of a tip-off?<br /> <br /> To be fair, my chronicle is painting the Orders in their worst possible light. My players agree with you: *even* at their best, the Orders are terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","user":"Justin Sane","date":". 09-07-2016, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T05:35:12-07:00","id":964907,"title":"","content":"Well, I always knew they were bad. I just didn't realize how bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T05:59:01-07:00","id":964913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964824#post964824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I \u200bget you but I'm thinking you don't understand my IRL mindset and what I would do if I actually were a mage and presented with the six choices. I believe anything good in life requires hard work and I my standards for myself are brutal. Hence I totally get and love the Silver Ladder and are disgusted by the Seers of the Throne. It isn't even a question to me. The Ladder uplifts and encourages everyone to be their best version of themselves. The Seers purposely keep you down because they don't want the competition. Greed, Envy, Jealousy and Sloth are typical Seer qualities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a matter of my not understanding your IRL mindset.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of me not trusting anyone who says &quot;I would never do that.&quot; Simply put, I've heard that too many times to actually believe it.<br /> <br /> I'm a Changeling fan, remember. If there is something I believe in, it's that a person's perspective can always radically change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy @#$#@. I take back everything I ever said. The implications of the Silver Ladder ideal is even worse than I ever imagined. Dear Goddess, the Ladder are officially some of the scariest people in the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're better than some, and I can even get behind their logic and on some days can even stand behind it.<br /> <br /> But there's a reason I was never that big of a fan of the Ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T06:47:03-07:00","id":964930,"title":"","content":"Well, its no secret I've never been a fan of most of the Orders in the first place. Its just... this is so much worse than I initially imagined it. And that's if we maintain that all Ladders are somehow striving for the ideal 24/7, which is never going to happen. Corruption is invariably going to leak into the system, and that's not even touching on mages that will have momentarily lapses or take things for granted, turning a blind eye, laze along, etc.<br /> <br /> And lets start adding on the &quot;worrying about hubris is for chumps!&quot; attitude many have....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T06:58:19-07:00","id":964937,"title":"","content":"Assuming they are striving for their ideal I'm not sure what the problem with wanting others to achieve their utmost potential is. Granted, they over value leadership, but other than that? It's not like they want to throw anyone not at the top in a gulag or crush them under oppression. Their ideal of leadership is generally the kind that serves others before themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:10:44-07:00","id":964940,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I'm not sure why the Ladder gets such a strong reaction. Mages existing brings up the exact same concerns; that people with unanswerable power will potentially use it in corrupt, selfish, or downright cruel ways. The Ladder is just a technocratic response to this situation and the only one that actually managed to set up a legal code and system to punish those who <i>do</i> act irresponsibly or maliciously.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm just a different sort of person but we already live in a world where the powerful have undeniable amounts of privilege and control over the poor and vulnerable. The horror already exists that someone could threaten, assault, or even kill you and get off with a slap on the wrist at worst; they just have to be a musician or perhaps a wealthy teen who claim that being privileged denied them an understanding of responsibility. We're only <i>just</i> out of an era where the sister of a President of the United States was lobotomized to the mental state of a two-year-old because she was &quot;troublesome&quot; for the family. This, all without the shadowy cabals of sorcerers who <i>do</i> exist in the World of Darkness and who can already wield their power to whatever end they wish.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder at least promises - and somewhat manages - a level of <i>noblesse oblige</i> as a part of their mandate, and comes with the unspoken guarantee that, since anyone can Awaken, the top echelons of their hierarchy will be diverse and drawn from a range of backgrounds and perspectives. We can't even get that in government now and the developed world has practiced democracy for how many centuries?<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder is horrifying because a world where there are unequal power dynamics is horrifying; because power is always and inevitably abused after being granted or acquired, be it in a day or in a century. We just already live in such a world, though, and the Ladder <i>has</i> to be compared to that pre-existing state of affairs. It can't just be thought of in isolation.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm just an apologist for technocratic autocracy, who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:51:01-07:00","id":964955,"title":"","content":"I believe it goes into what people feel about hierarchy itself.<br /> <br /> I would happily live in a Silver Ladder Society if it really ran like that. A society that enables and encourages one to be what they truly aspire to be? I'm in.<br /> <br /> I am all for freedom and self-determination. I believe in the essential value of each human being.<br /> <br /> But if you, under these utopian conditions, choose to do nothing productive for the society that makes this possible, excuse me while I don't take your opinion with as much consideration when deciding how to run the place.<br /> <br /> I don't let my broken (more than once) family parents to interfere in managing my household. I don't let a person who spent their resources on futility and ruined themselves make financial decisions for me. I won't refuse to listen to them, because bad experience is still experience, but the decision is not theirs. I will learn from their experience and will try, within my power, to make it better for myself and them.<br /> <br /> It is not about ignoring people as individual human beings. It is about knowing when that particular human being has no idea what he is talking about and you can't let that ignorance make things worse for everybody else. We're assuming the utopian society here, where the specialists know and love what their doing, and are peer reviewed to great standards.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, those who shy away from the Truth are passengers in the Reality boat.<br /> <br /> And to me that is fine. I don't want my stay at home mom wife piloting the jumbo jet we're in. I also don't want driven, workaholic, party hard work hard, never at home pilot lady raising my children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":".  grammerz 09-07-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:10:10-07:00","id":964961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964827#post964827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference, the Silver Ladder of Being:<br /> <i>-snip-</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this the sort of things we can look forward to in Tome of the Pentacle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:10:41-07:00","id":964962,"title":"","content":"For me, the saving grace of the Ladder - what seperates them from common-or-garden oligarchs - is their Obsession with social mobility. In our world, and even more so in the World of Darkness, we have countless people who could soar <i>so high</i> if they could only escape the circumstances of their birth. &quot;American Dream&quot; to the contrary, if you're poor but have the potential to be president or a heart surgeon you'll most likely languish in a dead-end job and die without ever realizing it. Our politicians bleat about opportunities and hold the vanishing exceptions up as proof that the system works, but really? Your average blue collar worker is a slave in all but name.<br /> <br /> The nature of Awakening is a near-random stroke of extreme good luck. The Ladder can't do anything about that (much as they honestly do want to) but that institutionalized inequality and static social class? They have that in their crosshairs, and every Illuminated cult is a weapon against it.<br /> <br /> They're just also paternalistic shitheads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:11:48-07:00","id":964963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964961#post964961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this the sort of things we can look forward to in Tome of the Pentacle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no. That's from the Silver Ladder Order book, from seven years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:12:48-07:00","id":964965,"title":"","content":"It would be nice to see a sample of the Illuminated cults, sort of what it would actually be like from the inside and out. Does the Silver Ladder book get into it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:18:24-07:00","id":964966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964704#post964704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean to ask: When someone knows they are not working for the greater good, they they are oppressive tyrants because that's how they roll, what do they tell themselves?<br /> <br /> That's the Seers of the Throne. They might have gone into it with altruistic motives, but then are quickly disabused of that notion. How?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This is the way the world is, and I can either get in line (and get mine) or I will get rolled over.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the core of Seer belief. You might have some who do <i>some things </i>altruistically, like keep watch over the fallen and Bound Old Gods, but even they know it's to keep the larger picture of Exarchal supremacy in line. It's a gang keeping other gangs under their thumb. Dress it up all you like, but you're running a protection racket on the china shop by keeping the bull's gate locked. <br /> <br /> From the religious perspective of serving the gods of the universe? The Seers are <i>well aware</i> that their gods are jealous gods. I don't think adding in the element of honest faith actually absolves the Seers of the need to be respectful to the agency of others. I'm a Roman Catholic, but I break with the Mother Church on a lot of things, especially Rome's treatment of gay and trans folks. Except <i>I'm</i> reasonably certain the Pope isn't scrying on me to make sure I fall the fuck in line, yeah?<br /> <br /> You might as well ask how a defense lawyer with a strong sense of ethics defends someone they suspect is a murderer, or a corporation they know full well is perpetrating a fraud. They do what they can to safeguard their Wisdom, they pride themselves on their excellent work, they tell themselves they didn't make the world this way, and they <i>take home their check</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 09-07-2016, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:40:38-07:00","id":964983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964930#post964930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, its no secret I've never been a fan of most of the Orders in the first place. Its just... this is so much worse than I initially imagined it. And that's if we maintain that all Ladders are somehow striving for the ideal 24/7, which is never going to happen. Corruption is invariably going to leak into the system, and that's not even touching on mages that will have momentarily lapses or take things for granted, turning a blind eye, laze along, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most thearchs are well aware of human nature, yes. They just think people can be better, and reality should be a meritocracy. You see elements of this in Arrow and Guardian beliefs, as well.<br /> <br /> (It's a quiet and subtle thing, but the Diamond Orders all have elements of each other's ethos deeply embedded in their core praxes)<br /> <br /> I really don't understand what's so bafflingly horrid about the idea that everyone should be able to choose their own destiny, and no one should be prevented from fulfilling themselves to the fullest of their ambition and ability. The Silver Ladder is totally down with a Star Trek-style post-scarcity society where Ben Sisko's dad runs a restaurant because he <i>really wants to run a restaurant </i>and he's <i>really good at it</i>, except the Ladder's is done with magic and the might of Imperium brimming in the soul of every human, because that's their <i>sovereign right.</i><br /> <br /> I <i>totally </i>get that most Ladders fall into the paternal shithead vibe of <i>telling you</i> what your proper fulfillment and place is, and they're often blind to their own hubris, but what Order isn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 09-07-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:59:51-07:00","id":964995,"title":"","content":"The talk about the Seers actually reminds me of an old ethics professor of mine who liked to talk a lot about how much easier it is to get into unethical situations by making decisions that are tempting but not immediately unethical. The man worked as a news room manager for about three decades and, in that time, saw a lot of people succumb to temptation.<br /> <br /> If you've built yourself up and manage to work your way to an anchor position, you might get offered 80,000 a year to work on some regional public network. There, you know that you have a mandate to provide actual news. Or you can take the 500,000 a year offer to go work for Fox, and I don't think I need to detail what that entails. The problem is, no-one <i>at the time of the offer</i> tells you precisely what you're going to have to do. You know what you'll have to do, it's certainly implied, but it's not in your face at that moment; only the money is. You get to become rich and famous instantly, with a guarantee of being able to publish book after book about your experiences; seeing the world, traveling to interesting places, and receiving a thousand and one kickbacks and rewards for your dutiful service. Your bosses will monitor your social media feeds, you'll be required to live your life a certain way, only use advertiser brands... But you'll be rich beyond the dreams of avarice and live a life that is exciting and interesting, albeit devoid of integrity.<br /> <br /> If someone said to a journalist &quot;I'll give you all that to compromise on this story&quot;, I imagine very few would agree. But when it's only an implication - a thought for you to deal with in the future - most will take the offer. If they didn't, we wouldn't have Fox, the Daily Mail, the Sun network...<br /> <br /> Humans prefer the immediate over the long term. Seers aren't told up front &quot;We'll give you ten grand if you go psychically torture those homeless people&quot;. They're given the rewards <i>first</i>; shown the glitz and glamour. When the office job begins, it's mostly benign. When the first real test of their integrity comes, the good things are already there and the bad things wait threateningly on the edges. Easier to stomp someone else's neck than put your own in the noose.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> But while I'm rambling, might as well share another point of view here: There's another major Seer motivator that's brought up periodically in the books but not ever really discussed and it's an important one when discussing the Silver Ladder: Fear.<br /> <br /> Power is not something people like to share. Willingly agreeing to give others power over yourself is the hardest thing to do. We don't like the idea of binding ourselves; of lashing ourselves to the wills of others. We ostensibly accept institutions that do so but usually only when they're out of sight. The thought of hearing people debate and vote on a bill in Congress or Parliament, or being close to an armed police officer, makes many people squirm, because these are both institutions which - albeit ostensibly serving them - have power over the individual which they have very little immediate ability to act against.<br /> <br /> Seers are jealous of power. They want <i>control</i>. They want the ability to orchestrate the world around them. Other people who are empowered in <i>any</i> way are a threat to that. The weaker everyone else is, the stronger the Seer. Every new Awakening is a new threat; a new godling challenging the Seer's supremacy. Keeping others down protects their hegemony; keeps them under the thumb of the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Thearchs walk a fine line in trying to do the opposite; to place an equal yoke around all necks. The Lex Magicka is impressive for the simple fact that it is a collective yielding of power by the Awakened to the polity, rather than maintaining absolute sovereignty. This doesn't seem so impressive to those of us who live under a government that is simply assumed to power by the weight of history, but every new Awakened is a sovereign individual; one that can ultimately likely do whatever they wish without ever fearing restriction. Joining that framework is a choice. That so many choose to do so must be a sign of the impressive power of the Lex and the Consilium system.<br /> <br /> It's as impressive a test of someone's nature when they're willing to give up power, perhaps as much so as what they do with it while they have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964965#post964965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be nice to see a sample of the Illuminated cults, sort of what it would actually be like from the inside and out. Does the Silver Ladder book get into it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. There's a fair chunk of a chapter dedicated to Cryptopolies and the Ladder's view of mystical hierarchy.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> - It amuses me to think that one of the Great Mysteries of the Universe is syndicalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:20:43-07:00","id":965002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964983#post964983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't understand what's so bafflingly horrid about the idea</div> </div> </div> </div> I think this conversation can easily be summed up with a Doctor Who quote from Army of Ghosts.<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0168554/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jackie Tyler</b></a>: You're always doing this, reducing it to science. Why couldn't it be real? Just think of it though: our families coming back home, all the people we've lost. Don't you think it's beautiful?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0855039/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Doctor</b></a>: I think it's horrific.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:28:00-07:00","id":965003,"title":"","content":"Not sure that flies, even if it had been possible it would have been a violation of the laws of time, it would have flown in the face of everything the Doctor knew about...everything.<br /> <br /> That isn't what the SL is doing though, it's trying to take the broken system of heirarchy that exists and fix it enough to actually give everyone a chance. It doesn't expect everyone to be happy, it expects everyone to have the chance to seize happiness for themselves.<br /> <br /> Y'know, it's fine if you don't like the SL, but it'd be nice if when a more nuanced interpretation of the SL than what you seem to be assuming (Boiled down, people in power =bad) if you'd actually say something new instead of pounding away at the same point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-07-2016, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:47:41-07:00","id":965012,"title":"","content":"People just really have different outlooks.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be opposed to a coming back of spirits past, if they were the Wise and Integral ones (not an extra-dimensional invasion force intent on conquering reality), and the continuum of space and time was maintained as to not invalidate our personal and shared history.<br /> <br /> I respect the past, but I don't let it chain the possibilities of the future. If it is demonstrably better than what we have, I'm open to it. I don't really care how much of a departure from the current state it is.<br /> <br /> A Silver Ladder to Awakening, to be climbed not because of your family, ethnicity, wealth or social standing, but because that is what your will is for yourself. That is what is on offer. And, to my view, that is demonstrably better than the Fallen Lie and the Reign of the Exarchs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":".  gramz 09-07-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:09:30-07:00","id":965025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965002#post965002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think this conversation can easily be summed up with a Doctor Who quote from Army of Ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think that flies, sorry. If your counterargument is that unlimited human agency will cause bad actors, enabled by the paternalistic grip of the Wise, that's what the Guardians are for. If you think humanity should be chained, there's an Order for that.<br /> <br /> (Serving the Throne out of misanthropy isn't altruism, though.)<br /> <br /> Maybe your argument is that the Ladder will cause Daleks to invade out of the Abyss? Or Scelesti, I guess? Sure, that's an inevitable bad result of &quot;The Awakened Are One Nation&quot;, but that also presumes the nation won't police those bad actors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:31:37-07:00","id":965047,"title":"","content":"What about where ability and ambition don't mesh? Plenty of people want to do things they're just flat-out bad at.<br /> <br /> I see two potential ways of handling this:<br /> <br /> Should someone's opinion be treated as less just because they aren't good at their job, despite wanting to be? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Should someone be treated as higher up the ladder than their talent allows for? That seems like a path to corruption in this system, when their ambition is &quot;power&quot; but their talents are more suited towards violence or something else lower on the totem pole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:40:18-07:00","id":965054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear;n96494<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder at least promises - and somewhat manages - a level of [I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">noblesse oblige[/I] as a part of their mandate, and comes with the <b>unspoken guarantee that, since anyone can Awaken,</b> the top echelons of their hierarchy will be diverse and drawn from a range of backgrounds and perspectives. We can't even get that in government now and the developed world has practiced democracy for how many centuries?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural beings other than mages cannot awaken, and I guess that explains one of the primary reasons why they're at the bottom of Dave's &quot;Silver Ladder of Being.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964966#post964966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might as well ask how a defense lawyer with a strong sense of ethics defends someone they suspect is a murderer, or a corporation they know full well is perpetrating a fraud. They do what they can to safeguard their Wisdom, they pride themselves on their excellent work, they tell themselves they didn't make the world this way, and they <i>take home their check</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a commercial litigator who's also engaged in a great deal of public interest work, the defense counsel analogy is inapt (and my pet peeve when lawyers are scapegoats or examples of greed and corruption).<br /> <br /> Representing a murderer or &quot;evil&quot; company is not a lapse in ethics and is not justified by lame excuses about &quot;how the world works&quot; or anything for a paycheck. The USA and most Western countries have an explicitly designed adversarial system of criminal and civil justice. Everyone is entitled to criminal defense and representation by counsel. Each lawyer is supposed to advocate <i>only</i> their client's interests, and any failure to do so is actually considered a serious breach of professional responsibility that could cost an attorney his or her license to practice law. <br /> <br /> To use the example of defending a murderer, I would first note it's usually the job of underpaid and overworked public defenders who, as a general matter, tend to hold decidedly liberal and progressive notions of social equality and economics. Under our system of justice, it's not enough to know your client may have committed the acts of which he's accused. Guilt is tested by the <i>State's</i> ability to <i>prove</i> it under accepted rules and procedures at trial. Despite what you may have seen on television, strict rules prevent lawyers from allowing perjury and other misconduct. Matters like innocent until proven guilty, a trial by one's peers, cross-examination of witnesses, clear rules of evidence, etc. are designed to protect people from oppression and tyranny, not promote it. Are there injustices, and are some attorneys better than others? Absolutely. However, these discrepancies exist with any system designed and implemented by imperfect humans. Like democracy as a form of government, such systems may be the worst form of justice, except for all the others.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm definitely in the mood to play a Silver Ladder mage who's an expert in the Lex Magica.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:47:12-07:00","id":965067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965047#post965047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about where ability and ambition don't mesh? Plenty of people want to do things they're just flat-out bad at.<br /> <br /> I see two potential ways of handling this:<br /> <br /> Should someone's opinion be treated as less just because they aren't good at their job, despite wanting to be? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that the proposed system is still a meritocracy, in terse term, yes. I am not going to take your opinion on these financial reports if you are bad at accounting, despite being an accountant. If you know someone to be a shitty cook, are you going to put more salt on the soup when they tell you to, just because they are a cook? I hope not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965047#post965047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should someone be treated as higher up the ladder than their talent allows for? That seems like a path to corruption in this system, when their ambition is &quot;power&quot; but their talents are more suited towards violence or something else lower on the totem pole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meritocracy again. If it works properly, it won't happen.<br /> <br /> On the ideal society, there are checks and balances, in the form of peers, institutions, and laws.<br /> <br /> Also note that the application of that violence, &quot;to keep order&quot; is essential to that position. Its not just being violent that counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:03:18-07:00","id":965077,"title":"","content":"Then it's about what people are good at, not what they want as claimed earlier, making it an oppressive hierarchy that unduly restricts personal freedoms based on circumstances of birth and chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:06:31-07:00","id":965081,"title":"","content":"No, the SL would prefer to guide you to a place you do want and where you do excel.<br /> <br /> Even despite that, it's unlikely they would force you unless you were an active danger. That doesn't mean you'd be respected or relied on for pursuing what you want when you're terrible at it. Which is basically exactly how things work now. If the cooks are bad the patrons won't eat there.<br /> <br /> You're jumping to the extreme unnecessarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:07:12-07:00","id":965082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965054#post965054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a commercial litigator who's also engaged in a great deal of public interest work, the defense counsel analogy is inapt (and my pet peeve when lawyers are scapegoats or examples of greed and corruption).<br /> <br /> Representing a murderer or &quot;evil&quot; company is not a lapse in ethics and is not justified by lame excuses about &quot;how the world works&quot; or anything for a paycheck. The USA and most Western countries have an explicitly designed adversarial system of criminal and civil justice. Everyone is entitled to criminal defense and representation by counsel. Each lawyer is supposed to advocate <i>only</i> their client's interests, and any failure to do so is actually considered a serious breach of professional responsibility that could cost an attorney his or her license to practice law.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand your frustrations - I think every field has its stereotypes that frustrate those within it; mechanics being treated as swindlers, bankers as cold and selfish, and so on.<br /> <br /> As far as a lapse of ethics goes, though, I think you're brushing against two very different philosophies here and two very different forms of moral culpability, which may actually be incompatible. It strikes me suddenly how curious it is that they're expected to co-exist.<br /> <br /> Justice commonly encompasses two ideals, one being that a person should do their utmost to ensure that the guilty are found to be so and made to answer for their crimes, the other that everyone deserves their day in court and the utmost defenses due to the law. The problem is, you can't actually be a lawyer doing the latter without potentially violating the former. A lawyer who defends a client they know is guilty cannot do both; they cannot simultaneously ensure that their client has their rights protected while also doing their utmost to ensure that the guilty are sentenced to be so. Indeed, they abnegate that duty to properly serve their client. At the same time, they can't just tell the police &quot;My client confessed to me&quot; without violating the rights they are due before the law.<br /> <br /> This is without even touching on the other issue; that someone who takes a retainer from a company they know to engage in unethical practices without any guarantee that said company will <i>cease</i> said unethical practices openly and knowingly agrees to provide shelter and advice - albeit within the law - for how their client can avoid reforming their ways.<br /> <br /> There's no resolution to this, I don't think, that doesn't introduce entirely new conflicts of interest to the system, but the Silver Ladder seems to try and solve it with the institution of Lictor; judge, jury, and investigator, rolled into one. Even so, the adversarial system is maintained in many regions.<br /> <br /> I feel the need to add that I have the utmost respect for litigators - as I could probably say for just about any profession - and intend nothing in this as disrespectful; just an observation on the disparate ideals hidden within the common notion of justice; one that really doesn't allow a &quot;win&quot; scenario for lawyers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:14:37-07:00","id":965095,"title":"","content":"I've always considered it an implicitly held stance of the Silver Ladder that once humanity has a firm grasp of the Imperium, situations like &quot;my body and/or mind isn't good enough to let me pursue my dreams&quot; will become somewhat of a non-issue.<br /> <br /> The Ladder of Being is about shaping all of reality, including humans themselves, with the end goal being humans able to express themselves to their fullest desire. There is no reason why the individual's natural talents (or rather the lack of them) shouldn't be treated as a deficiency to be improved upon, with Imperial magic if it comes to that. It may start with cutting off Sleepers' ties to the Abyss on a personal level and eliminating the Abyss and Exarchs on a cosmic scale, but it doesn't have to end there. At that point, Pax Arcanum won't really exist anymore.<br /> <br /> Remember, Thearchs consider *any* pain, any itch in the nose an offense toward mankind. How do you think they'll treat, say, clumsiness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-07-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:32:19-07:00","id":965119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965081#post965081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the SL would prefer to guide you to a place you do want and where you do excel.<br /> <br /> Even despite that, it's unlikely they would force you unless you were an active danger. That doesn't mean you'd be respected or relied on for pursuing what you want when you're terrible at it. Which is basically exactly how things work now. If the cooks are bad the patrons won't eat there.<br /> <br /> You're jumping to the extreme unnecessarily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact, Dave addressed how Thearchs basically address these issues as a practical matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964848#post964848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to why certain types of people are on higher or lower rungs of the Ladder, according to orthodox thearchs:<br /> <br /> It's about the responsibility of the enlightened to give guidance to those less enlightened. That's why it goes mage-priest-technocrat-manager-bully-famous-follower-monster.<br /> <br /> Clavigers tell student thearchs not to apply these classifications on face value (is a musician influential because she's a truly excellent composer-songwriter, or because she win pop idol? Is a businessman an actual good manager dedicated to his employee's interests, or a bullying blowhard? Is a priest just mouthing doctrine, or does she genuinely tens to spiritual needs of her followers?)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:03:48-07:00","id":965161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965077#post965077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it's about what people are good at, not what they want as claimed earlier, making it an oppressive hierarchy that unduly restricts personal freedoms based on circumstances of birth and chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is you are free to reach for what you want. You are free to climb the Ladder. There is no guarantee you will be good at or happy with what you achieve.<br /> <br /> You are free to improve yourself. And those in the Ladder will work so that you have what you need to rise. But it is still on you.<br /> <br /> You are taking an exclusivity stance here, when you should look at it inclusively. It is about both, freedom and merit, mobility and excellence. Not one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:34:00-07:00","id":965186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964966#post964966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;This is the way the world is, and I can either get in line (and get mine) or I will get rolled over.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the core of Seer belief. You might have some who do <i>some things </i>altruistically, like keep watch over the fallen and Bound Old Gods, but even they know it's to keep the larger picture of Exarchal supremacy in line. It's a gang keeping other gangs under their thumb. Dress it up all you like, but you're running a protection racket on the china shop by keeping the bull's gate locked.<br /> <br /> From the religious perspective of serving the gods of the universe? The Seers are <i>well aware</i> that their gods are jealous gods. I don't think adding in the element of honest faith actually absolves the Seers of the need to be respectful to the agency of others. I'm a Roman Catholic, but I break with the Mother Church on a lot of things, especially Rome's treatment of gay and trans folks. Except <i>I'm</i> reasonably certain the Pope isn't scrying on me to make sure I fall the fuck in line, yeah?<br /> <br /> You might as well ask how a defense lawyer with a strong sense of ethics defends someone they suspect is a murderer, or a corporation they know full well is perpetrating a fraud. They do what they can to safeguard their Wisdom, they pride themselves on their excellent work, they tell themselves they didn't make the world this way, and they <i>take home their check</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with your lawyer analogy for the reasons expressed later by another in this thread.<br /> <br /> And I agree with you on everything else. What you described doesn't require any sort of delusional thinking or &quot;True Believer&quot; type of mentality. It's people doing bad things in order to protect themselves from worse things. It goes hand-in-hand with Fear as also enumerated in this thread by another contributor.<br /> <br /> The Seers are like the party from 1984. They are priests of power, existing only to trample and be trampled upon. It all gets explained in the book when O'Brien tortures Winston.<br /> <br /> I don't need the Seers of the Throne to be people who believe they are the good guys. I don't need to be able to empathize with them or identify with them. I don't need them to be player characters (although, I've got no qualms with folks who do like to play Seers). It's not how I roll. People like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"191\" data-vbnamecard=\"191\">Strill</a> would disagreed with me, but in this game it doesn't matter one iota what a mage <i>thinks</i>. <i><b>What matters is what a mage does.</b></i> Seers of the Throne are evil, selfish, fearful bastards because they do evil, selfish, fearful things. That's fine with me.<br /> <br /> The other Orders, <i>especially</i> the Silver Ladder and Guardians of the Veil (and Free Council), can be &quot;True Believers&quot; who think they are good guys even when they do bad things. I can relate to that. I can empathize with that. Those sorts of people can be reasoned with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:36:16-07:00","id":965187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965002#post965002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think this conversation can easily be summed up with a Doctor Who quote from Army of Ghosts.<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0168554/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jackie Tyler</b></a>: You're always doing this, reducing it to science. Why couldn't it be real? Just think of it though: our families coming back home, all the people we've lost. Don't you think it's beautiful?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0855039/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Doctor</b></a>: I think it's horrific.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I find that quote funny comming from the most shown hippocrite incarnation of the doctor.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wont use guns! But if you piss me off is eternal punishment for you......good guy(?)&quot;<br /> <br /> Even in one of the last episodes they point that out and the show completely ignore it because the doctor had to be the good guy<br /> <br /> &quot;<i><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0088045/\" target=\"_blank\">Davros</a></i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The man who abhors violence, never carrying a gun, but this is the truth, Doctor: you take ordinary people and you fashion them into weapons... behold your Children of Time, transformed into murderers. I made the Daleks, Doctor, you made this.</span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> But that aside, the quote doesnt make that much sense in the context of this.....or at least not a clear sense. Care to expand?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-07-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:31:59-07:00","id":965399,"title":"","content":"See, I agree with the thearchs that people have their place in the world and would be best finding it and fulfilling themselves with it. Not everyone is supposed to the rock star and movie god. If burger flipping is what you're good at and it makes you happy, then by all means, be the best damn burger flipper in your neighborhood.<br /> <br /> It's the entire &quot;I know where you belong&quot; attitude that makes me....Well. I'm careful about who I trust the reins of my life to as much as I can be, we'll leave it at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-07-2016, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T18:59:28-07:00","id":965410,"title":"","content":"One suddenly has to be curious what the opinions of all the people in this thread about putting people in rehab programs for drug use/addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:03:29-07:00","id":965413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965410#post965410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One suddenly has to be curious what the opinions of all the people in this thread about putting people in rehab programs for drug use/addiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, nothing's ever easy. Just because I'm wary doesn't mean I'm completely against. They just rub me the wrong way regardless of their good points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:08:37-07:00","id":965414,"title":"","content":"From the Silver Ladder's standpoint, what happens when a manager decides they want to be a mage? Or, why stop there, why not an Oracle, so they can be at the top? Not because they're good at it, but because they want that power.<br /> <br /> Presumably those above making decisions is a safety switch against another group deciding they would prefer being Exarchs lording over everyone.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's possible the Order book gets into it more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:12:00-07:00","id":965415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965410#post965410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One suddenly has to be curious what the opinions of all the people in this thread about putting people in rehab programs for drug use/addiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big believer in informed consent for all medical or psychological practice. The only exception, which should be used very rarely and even then only justifying the minimal intervention necessary, is if it can be established that the person is incapable of making decisions themselves for whatever reason. Extreme addiction can potentially cross that line and justify involuntary treatment in some cases, but it's something we need to be very careful about.<br /> <br /> What's the comparison between that and the Silver Ladder? I can't quite piece the connection together myself, so I'm curious what parallel you're drawing between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:57:19-07:00","id":965438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965413#post965413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be fair, nothing's ever easy. Just because I'm wary doesn't mean I'm completely against. They just rub me the wrong way regardless of their good points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It's just fun to highlight the trust issues inherent in the Silver Ladder's mandate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965415#post965415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big believer in informed consent for all medical or psychological practice. The only exception, which should be used very rarely and even then only justifying the minimal intervention necessary, is if it can be established that the person is incapable of making decisions themselves for whatever reason. Extreme addiction can potentially cross that line and justify involuntary treatment in some cases, but it's something we need to be very careful about.<br /> <br /> What's the comparison between that and the Silver Ladder? I can't quite piece the connection together myself, so I'm curious what parallel you're drawing between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say there's a pretty direct comparison between the Quiescence and addiction. Both are conditions that addle the mind and deprive the sufferer of the ability to properly perceive the world. Both are conditions which force the sufferer to reject aid, no matter how dearly they might want it. Both limit the &quot;natural&quot; functioning of a human being.<br /> <br /> Thearchs live in a world of people like that; people who cannot see the Truth and who, indeed, actively recoil from it. Thearchs cannot possibly get informed consent from Sleepers because Sleepers cannot possibly know what they are consenting to; the transformative act of Awakening utterly separates the enlightened from the masses.<br /> <br /> Similar comparisons can be made to developmental disabilities, where someone with a mental handicap might refuse treatments that could potentially assist them in living a normal life or at least a healthier, easier, and more independent one. Can such a person be considered to have the capacity for informed consent to a treatment whose outcome they can scarcely fathom?<br /> <br /> Consent is a concept that really grinds and sparks when there is a differential in power and capacity for understanding between the provider and subject. With the Awakened and the Sleeping masses, that differential is extreme. The Ladder seems to assume that it's extreme enough that informed consent is either impossible or that bringing the world closer to Hieraconis is sufficiently important that it is not necessary. Maybe both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:56:06-07:00","id":965462,"title":"","content":"Of course, that's all only valid if Mages are <i>right</i>. They have their perspective on the world, but they can't be sure their perspective is the correct one.<br /> <br /> Awakening comes with more power and the ability to see reality through different lenses than anyone else, but those lenses aren't necessarily correct or even better.<br /> <br /> You can't really prove that the Supernal is the &quot;right&quot; world any more than the Shadow or the Underworld are. Looking at the things that live there really make me question whether it's any better there at all.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder are assuming their way is the right and better way, and they can't really ever be sure of that. That's pretty dangerous and not at all admirable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:24:37-07:00","id":965476,"title":"","content":"Mages don't have to be right at all about the nature of Truth for them to argue that their perspective is wider than that of ordinary Sleepers. That's pretty self-evident by dint of them simply being Mages; beings who are not only aware of other realms of existence and the fundamental structure of reality but capable of exploring and manipulating them. Mages can claim that they are to Sleepers as the seeing are to the blind a thousand times over, and they can back it up.<br /> <br /> Even if that weren't the case, your response is basically reductive relativism; that there is no objective morality or good. Even assuming you're correct there - and the game doesn't necessarily assume you are - you're not offering an alternative that the exact same question cannot be asked of. Whenever we make any decision, take <i>any</i> course of action, we are making a statement and affirmation of the beliefs and ideas that go into that decision. Even choosing not to take one's own life every waking moment is such a decision and such a declaration. You make, with every single breath, the declaration and assumption that your way is the right and better way simply by not picking the alternative.<br /> <br /> You can't make a statement that this is all perspective, not factual reality, then condemn them for subjective judgements like danger and worthiness. You either have to point out contradiction in derivations of their premises or disagree with the premises themselves. If you don't like the Ladder's humanism, that's fine, but you can't treat their assumptions as any more or less founded than your own.<br /> <br /> Likewise, you can't make statements about lack of access to absolute truth. Mages may not have absolute certainty that the Supernal is what they think it is, but they don't have absolute certainty that they're not a brain in a vat experiencing a computer simulation, or that all of this is a dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:35:07-07:00","id":965482,"title":"","content":"You are reading a whole lot more into my post than is actually there. You are also inferring a great many things with no evidence to support them whatsoever. Your post is so devoid of coherent logic that I'm struggling to develop a proper response.<br /> <br /> I will try again in the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:37:37-07:00","id":965483,"title":"","content":"Sometimes you just have to take what you know and work with it. The Silver Ladder isn't alone in that, the other Orders all have beliefs that may not pan out, even the Seers. Maybe there is no true upward mobility, maybe there is no possible way to defeat the Seers, or bring about a substantial increase in Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> Arguably it's detrimental to bend all of the Awakened to these ideas, but sitting around waiting for the answers before trying isn't going to get anyone anywhere either. And it's not as if their theories are the only things the Orders have managed to bring to the table. Through the Silver Ladder's ideas, they've managed to form mages into a fairly cohesive society with laws and structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:47:27-07:00","id":965508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=964913#post964913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a matter of my not understanding your IRL mindset.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of me not trusting anyone who says &quot;I would never do that.&quot; Simply put, I've heard that too many times to actually believe it.<br /> <br /> I'm a Changeling fan, remember. If there is something I believe in, it's that a person's perspective can always radically change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're better than some, and I can even get behind their logic and on some days can even stand behind it.<br /> <br /> But there's a reason I was never that big of a fan of the Ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't believe it. Jus\u200bt accept I'm telling you the truth and that I'm nowhere near 20 and have a low opinion of humanity and people in general. Also I'm going off years of real life experience about just how venal people can be if given the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T23:27:31-07:00","id":965518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965415#post965415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a big believer in informed consent for all medical or psychological practice. The only exception, which should be used very rarely and even then only justifying the minimal intervention necessary, is if it can be established that the person is incapable of making decisions themselves for whatever reason. Extreme addiction can potentially cross that line and justify involuntary treatment in some cases, but it's something we need to be very careful about.<br /> <br /> What's the comparison between that and the Silver Ladder? I can't quite piece the connection together myself, so I'm curious what parallel you're drawing between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Sleepers are by definition incapable of making informed choices about magic. That's where they fall down - and recognise that they fall down.<br /> <br /> The Ladder's attitude to people they think act against their scheme is interesting and illuminating - if a Sleeper is ruining the lives of those they have misplaced authority over, the Ladder prefers to show them the error of their ways by arranging positive reinforcement. The bad boss gets hooked by a taste of whatever they're lacking (say, membership in a club, or something in their life fixed) and then some advice from an Illuminate (a NonAwakened member of one of the Order's mystery cults) - if they follow the advice, they get more good things. Eventually, the situation is fixed in a virtuous circle without the illuminate - or the mage behind her - needing to play an active role any more, and the now-good boss becomes an illuminate. And the Ladder looks for the next dysfunctional system to repair.<br /> <br /> This only applies to Sleepers, because Sleepers don't know any better and can't be expected to without guidance (though those that do are praiseworthy). <i>Mages</i>, though... A tyrannical Hierarch will enjoy the Ladder trying to advise them into better systems for a while, but eventually the Order will take Steps. Even if they're in the Ladder. Especially if they're in the Ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T02:43:19-07:00","id":965571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965482#post965482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are reading a whole lot more into my post than is actually there. You are also inferring a great many things with no evidence to support them whatsoever. Your post is so devoid of coherent logic that I'm struggling to develop a proper response.<br /> <br /> I will try again in the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually he made perfect sense. Basically, you have your perspective on the world, but you can't be sure your perspective is the correct one. Your argument can be turned back on itself, you can't prove the SL are wrong and that's pretty dangerous and not at all admirable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-08-2016, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:28:07-07:00","id":965594,"title":"","content":"Let's give this a shot, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965476#post965476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages don't have to be right at all about the nature of Truth for them to argue that their perspective is wider than that of ordinary Sleepers. That's pretty self-evident by dint of them simply being Mages; beings who are not only aware of other realms of existence and the fundamental structure of reality but capable of exploring and manipulating them. Mages can claim that they are to Sleepers as the seeing are to the blind a thousand times over, and they can back it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is partly true. But mages are remarkably limited in outlook as well. When it comes to Knowing things, their entire perspective is through the lens of the Supernal. There is plenty the Supernal can't answer for. Pretending you have all the answers when you only have some, even if that's more than most people, is irresponsible and ignorant at its most benevolent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965476#post965476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if that weren't the case, your response is basically reductive relativism; that there is no objective morality or good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please quote where I said anything of the sort. If there is objective morality or good, then <i>mages do not know it</i>. Indeed, Wisdom allows for a whole lot of actions that many would consider morally wrong. I mean, it's kind of objective in the CofD that morality is subjective. That's why every splat has a different set of standards, though this has changed a lot in 2e. But it's still not relevant to my earlier argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965476#post965476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even assuming you're correct there - and the game doesn't necessarily assume you are - you're not offering an alternative that the exact same question cannot be asked of. Whenever we make any decision, take <i>any</i> course of action, we are making a statement and affirmation of the beliefs and ideas that go into that decision. Even choosing not to take one's own life every waking moment is such a decision and such a declaration. You make, with every single breath, the declaration and assumption that your way is the right and better way simply by not picking the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the bit that blew my mind the most. There is no rational argument here. Nothing here approaches reality in any way. Nobody picks what they believe to be the &quot;best&quot; option 100% of the time. Having been suicidal, any number of things can prevent it even if you genuinely believe the better option is to die. Things like lack of opportunity, fear of death, the survival instinct. Look at the talk about Seers earlier. Greed and fear and threats and blackmail can all keep people from doing what they think is the &quot;best&quot; option. And there is a <i>huge</i> leap between &quot;I think this is the best option&quot; and &quot;I'm going to make everyone else conform to my personal view of what's best for reality.&quot; That's where the Silver Ladder are wrong. They're wanting to impose their remarkably limited view on all of reality. Including putting people on the bottom of the rung due to no fault of their own, due to circumstances outside their own control. Most supernaturals in CofD don't choose their condition. Even the ones that can aren't always given the choice. A vampire that was turned by force can never, ever reach self-actualization in the Silver Ladder's system. Neither can a Changeling, whose only crime was getting kidnapped and escaping from their kidnapper. A Sin-Eater is given less say on matters of death than a hobo on the street despite knowing it more intimately and naturally than a Moros Master of Death.<br /> <br /> This is a worldview based on the supreme hubris of &quot;We are right and everyone else is wrong, we know everything and you know nothing.&quot; The only thing resembling a saving grace is &quot;We'll teach you our approved curriculum if you like&quot; which doesn't matter if the curriculum is severely lacking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965476#post965476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't make a statement that this is all perspective, not factual reality, then condemn them for subjective judgements like danger and worthiness. You either have to point out contradiction in derivations of their premises or disagree with the premises themselves. If you don't like the Ladder's humanism, that's fine, but you can't treat their assumptions as any more or less founded than your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between my assumptions and theirs is that I'm not trying to rewrite reality based on my own incomplete understanding. This is the point that you aren't getting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965476#post965476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, you can't make statements about lack of access to absolute truth. Mages may not have absolute certainty that the Supernal is what they think it is, but they don't have absolute certainty that they're not a brain in a vat experiencing a computer simulation, or that all of this is a dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're just being intellectually dishonest. The Supernal not being what Mages think it is just because they visited it once for a few moments is not equivalent at all. Just because two things haven't been proven doesn't mean they share equal levels of proof or evidence. And just because you have evidence for something doesn't mean you aren't interpreting that evidence incorrectly.<br /> <br /> Mages know that there is a Supernal. They know that when it interacts with the world we live in, adverse reactions take place that they call Abyssal. The consensus is that this means that this is some sort of Gnostic fallen world, leading to lovely ideas full of hubris like Mages being filled with the spark of the divine. That doesn't mean that this interpretation is correct, and the evidence is far from conclusive. Especially when the Supernal can't cover half of what happens down here in the real world.<br /> <br /> And the problem is when a group of mages take this as gospel and set about trying to change reality to match this interpretation, no matter what their future subjects want, because they aren't &quot;enlightened&quot; enough to have a say. Even most of the other &quot;enlightened&quot; ones aren't allowed to have a say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:32:15-07:00","id":965596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965571#post965571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually he made perfect sense. Basically, you have your perspective on the world, but you can't be sure your perspective is the correct one. Your argument can be turned back on itself, you can't prove the SL are wrong and that's pretty dangerous and not at all admirable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Look up <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophic_burden_of_proof\" target=\"_blank\">Burden of Proof</a> so that you can actually contribute. People are asserting that the Silver Ladder world view is worth imposing on everyone, whether they like it or not. I dispute this assertion. I am not imposing my view on everyone, unlike what the Silver Ladder would attempt if they could. These are not equivalent situations in the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T05:16:55-07:00","id":965612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965518#post965518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This only applies to Sleepers, because Sleepers don't know any better and can't be expected to without guidance (though those that do are praiseworthy). <i>Mages</i>, though... A tyrannical Hierarch will enjoy the Ladder trying to advise them into better systems for a while, but eventually the Order will take Steps. Even if they're in the Ladder. Especially if they're in the Ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under their fundamental ideology, will the SL takes &quot;Steps&quot; against other supernaturals who are not Sleepers (e.g., vampires, werewolves, etc.) if they abuse their authority. <br /> <br /> If so, it would appear that somewhat fundamentalist SL mages would make great hunter/antagonist npc's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:07:59-07:00","id":965625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965508#post965508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't believe it. Jus\u200bt accept I'm telling you the truth and that I'm nowhere near 20 and have a low opinion of humanity and people in general. Also I'm going off years of real life experience about just how venal people can be if given the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You do recognize the irony of &quot;Just accept I'm telling you the truth&quot; in this thread, right? Hell, on this specific topic even.<br /> <br /> 2) Funny how we're in different positions. I am over 20, have a high opinion of humanity and people in general* (AND I work in a call center, wrap your head around that), and I am also going off years of experience of seeing people commit their &quot;I would nevers&quot;. Fuck, I'm one of them.<br /> <br /> So, no. You keep believing you won't-that's how you avoid it-and I'll hope you can keep it.<br /> <br /> But I won't believe it.<br /> <br /> *And yes, this does still factor in I imagine a majority of people would be Seers if they Awakened. Even then, I believe in my species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:49:51-07:00","id":965639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965596#post965596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look up <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophic_burden_of_proof&amp;quot;]Burden</a> of Proof[/URL] so that you can actually contribute. People are asserting that the Silver Ladder world view is worth imposing on everyone, whether they like it or not. I dispute this assertion. I am not imposing my view on everyone, unlike what the Silver Ladder would attempt if they could. These are not equivalent situations in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that assertion was made, simply that their system isn't without merit. Is it perfect? No, even the SL don't think that, they have built systems of governance and ideology from the ground up more than once and will take it in stride if they have to do it again.<br /> <br /> From outside the game it's easy to see how the Ladder could run into problems, from the inside of their magic humanocentric viewpoint? Probably not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:35:20-07:00","id":965662,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965596#post965596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look up <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophic_burden_of_proof\" target=\"_blank\">Burden of Proof</a> so that you can actually contribute. People are asserting that the Silver Ladder world view is worth imposing on everyone, whether they like it or not. I dispute this assertion. I am not imposing my view on everyone, unlike what the Silver Ladder would attempt if they could. These are not equivalent situations in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, before I go any further, I need to address this: Thus far, you've come off as fairly aggressive and combative to me and other people in the thread. I don't mind when people are to me, but I don't like it when it's directed to other people.<br /> <br /> Not trying to be aggressive here either. Just... Friendly discussion, yeah?<br /> <br /> We'll return to the other thing you said here later on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965594#post965594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is partly true. But mages are remarkably limited in outlook as well. When it comes to Knowing things, their entire perspective is through the lens of the Supernal. There is plenty the Supernal can't answer for. Pretending you have all the answers when you only have some, even if that's more than most people, is irresponsible and ignorant at its most benevolent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's neither the point, nor asserted. It's not that the Silver Ladder claims they're omniscient, just that they're <i>more</i> knowledgeable than Sleepers and, indeed, are so by far. That isn't really open to dispute, nor is that this knowledge makes them exceptionally more capable. Where a legitimate point of dispute lies is in what standard shall we judge their social system and mandate and membership by; and, from that, whether they are better than any others.<br /> <br /> There's certainly an argument to be made that the Ladder are just imperialist assholes, but whether or not the Awakened are more aware or capable than mundane mortals isn't really open for discussion. Just because they're not omnipotent or omniscient or may have biases does not <i>change</i> that fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965594#post965594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please quote where I said anything of the sort. If there is objective morality or good, then <i>mages do not know it</i>. Indeed, Wisdom allows for a whole lot of actions that many would consider morally wrong. I mean, it's kind of objective in the CofD that morality is subjective. That's why every splat has a different set of standards, though this has changed a lot in 2e. But it's still not relevant to my earlier argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a reason I said &quot;basically&quot;. Your post largely boiled down to &quot;They can't be certain they're right&quot;, which is more or less relativism in a nutshell; a claim that no moral argument can be put forth strongly because there can be no certainty of its absolute correctness.<br /> <br /> My answer to this is that you have to argue against premises, not merely try to dismiss it. There may just be a misunderstanding here, though; that you were attacking any form of Supernalism and not merely being relativist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965594#post965594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the bit that blew my mind the most. There is no rational argument here. Nothing here approaches reality in any way. Nobody picks what they believe to be the &quot;best&quot; option 100% of the time. -snip-<br /> <br /> This is a worldview based on the supreme hubris of &quot;We are right and everyone else is wrong, we know everything and you know nothing.&quot; The only thing resembling a saving grace is &quot;We'll teach you our approved curriculum if you like&quot; which doesn't matter if the curriculum is severely lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is where you and I depart philosophically: People are rarely, if ever, offered perfectly optimal choices, but I do not believe they are freed from the moral weight of those choices. Choosing the lesser of two evils is still a choice, and whatever choice is made is one which reflects the values and beliefs of the chooser, regardless of anything else.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean for one instant that I believe there is an automatic moral failing for such choices. Someone who steals to feed their starving children does not, in my mind, deserve any punishment (with the usual caveats, etc. etc.), but they have made statements by their actions: That survival comes before respect for property; that the lives of their children matter more than the finances of the baker; that living matters more to them than law. Personally, I'd give a thumbs up in this circumstance, but that's not the point. The point is that, just by their actions, they have made a silent declaration that they believe all those things to be true. Whether or not they might consciously affirm them, their actions are a statement that they clearly believe them enough to act upon them.<br /> <br /> I do not believe that life is without opportunity costs. I do not believe that there is an automatic &quot;null&quot; option when it comes to living. I believe every action, every choice, is a statement of belief, be it consciously acknowledged or not, and that brings me into the next point which - usefully - allows me to answer your very next statement as well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965594#post965594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference between my assumptions and theirs is that I'm not trying to rewrite reality based on my own incomplete understanding. This is the point that you aren't getting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>are</i> rewriting reality based on your incomplete understanding. Not (necessarily) on the large scale, but you're always doing it for someone; something. Every time you speak with a person, you change their world just a little. Every stroke of your keys here is changing the universe, ever so slightly. The actions you take now are irreversible and unchangeable. The energy lost to entropy as you use your computer will vanish into random molecular motion in deep space, never to be turned to any useful purpose ever again. The system of governance you support will determine and dictate the styles of living not merely of people within your country but those beyond it; millions, tens of millions, hundreds of millions of people affected, even if you ostensibly support whatever governance you consider &quot;most free&quot;.<br /> <br /> Every time you vote, any business you might run, every book you write, every political office you might one day hold, any job you do, every purchase you make, you change the world and this is inescapable truth.<br /> <br /> The only difference between you and them is scale.<br /> <br /> (The Ladder's attitude towards the Terata is, incidentally, fairly bigoted. I just wanted to address Hubris and philosophical differences.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965594#post965594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you're just being intellectually dishonest. The Supernal not being what Mages think it is just because they visited it once for a few moments is not equivalent at all. Just because two things haven't been proven doesn't mean they share equal levels of proof or evidence. And just because you have evidence for something doesn't mean you aren't interpreting that evidence incorrectly.<br /> <br /> Mages know that there is a Supernal. They know that when it interacts with the world we live in, adverse reactions take place that they call Abyssal. The consensus is that this means that this is some sort of Gnostic fallen world, leading to lovely ideas full of hubris like Mages being filled with the spark of the divine. That doesn't mean that this interpretation is correct, and the evidence is far from conclusive. Especially when the Supernal can't cover half of what happens down here in the real world.<br /> <br /> And the problem is when a group of mages take this as gospel and set about trying to change reality to match this interpretation, no matter what their future subjects want, because they aren't &quot;enlightened&quot; enough to have a say. Even most of the other &quot;enlightened&quot; ones aren't allowed to have a say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to ask if you've read Imperial Mysteries before addressing any of the talk about the Supernal. If you said it about Atlantis and their mystical origin story, we'd be in more agreement, but the Supernal itself isn't so up for dispute.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I don't really <i>want</i> to list the evidences Mages have for believing what they do because it echoes too much of Mage Supremacy. Just the same, an important correction is that most Mages don't believe the Supernal <i>interacts</i> with the Fallen World so much as <i>sustains</i> it; that the Fallen World is a product of Supernal Truth. As evidence of this, they'd point to things like the Tapestry being constructed of Mana; the very substance of the Supernal.)<br /> <br /> Mages taking their self-declared holiness as gospel and saying &quot;We are the Homo superior; we get to be kings&quot; being the problem - the whole fun part that gives this drama - is something we can agree on, though. <i>That's</i> where the Ladder becomes fun, to my mind. Not of questions of whether their cosmology is necessarily correct, but whether dictatorship can ever truly be benevolent; whether imperialism can ever <i>actually</i> be an uplifting force, or whether it's just enslavement in golden chains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:48:07-07:00","id":965673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965625#post965625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Funny how we're in different positions. I am over 20, have a high opinion of humanity and people in general* (AND I work in a call center, wrap your head around that), and I am also going off years of experience of seeing people commit their &quot;I would nevers&quot;. Fuck, I'm one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I should say so myself, I don't <i>believe</i> I would be a Seer, for ideological and religious reasons, and the fact that I am a very very devout Gnostic who would like any opressive gods to take their leave please, and <i>even </i>then I think I could probably see myself in a nice suit in Unity honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:06:41-07:00","id":965685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965673#post965673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I should say so myself, I don't <i>believe</i> I would be a Seer, for ideological and religious reasons, and the fact that I am a very very devout Gnostic who would like any opressive gods to take their leave please, and <i>even </i>then I think I could probably see myself in a nice suit in Unity honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a litany of personal reasons, I, too, don't believe I would ever willingly choose to be a Seer. <br /> <br /> However, never forget that the Seers are VERY good at what they do, and have perfected their sales and recruitment pitch over centuries. <br /> <br /> First, new mages are often not even aware of the different Orders or the depravity and corruption of the Exarchs and Seers. As far a newly Awakened mages are concerned, the only choice may be to join the Seers, the only fellowship of mages they know, or try to survive is a cold and hostile new world. Sometimes there really isn't any real choice. <br /> <br /> Second, and more importantly, the Seers effectively use both the carrot and the stick. Under certain circumstances, you might not have a choice but to join. The Exarchs are real, the Seers have great magical and temporal power, and they can indeed do great harm to you and those you care about if defied. <br /> <br /> Third, they are able to offer mages not only mundane wealth beyond avarice, but tremendous magical resources and training. Many people with great and honorable ideals throughout history have been seduced by wealth and power. In the real world, even the best people succumb to temptation. With the aid of magic, I can only imagine how impressive the gifts of the Seers are to a new mage, particularly one who did not know such luxury in the prior Fallen lives.<br /> <br /> I'm told you've never really lived until you've partied with the Seers. The drugs and whores really are that good... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T09:34:27-07:00","id":965718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965054#post965054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm definitely in the mood to play a Silver Ladder mage who's an expert in the Lex Magica.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you somewhat missed the point of what I was saying, which is that a lawyer\u2019s right (and ethical duty) to engage in zealous advocacy only extends as far as that advocacy is constructive in the support of justice within the adversarial legal system. ...but you want to play a Silver Ladder out of it, and I admit I only touched on that argument rather than actually making it, so it's all good. If you want a better and less stereotypical example of what I meant, the Boston Globe ran a <i>very</i> good story a few years back about lawyers who specialize in OUI cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:21:42-07:00","id":965759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965718#post965718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you somewhat missed the point of what I was saying, which is that a lawyer\u2019s right (and ethical duty) to engage in zealous advocacy only extends as far as that advocacy is constructive in the support of justice within the adversarial legal system. ...but you want to play a Silver Ladder out of it, and I admit I only touched on that argument rather than actually making it, so it's all good. If you want a better and less stereotypical example of what I meant, the Boston Globe ran a <i>very</i> good story a few years back about lawyers who specialize in OUI cases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First, as a general matter, I'm certainly not claiming lawyers or the practice of law is somehow inherently virtuous. There are good lawyers and bad, travesties of justice and outcomes that most would consider both procedurally and substantially fair. Every lawyer and case should be judged on their own merits. I simply take issue with attorneys as the &quot;go to&quot; examples of greed or corruption. Without singling you out, as you obviously meant no offense, it's a lazy stereotype that belittles the hard work, dedication, professionalism, and competence of an entire profession that includes people who hold the entire spectrum of political, social, economic and other views.<br /> <br /> However, as another poster observed with my original comment, the examples you offered about the some well publicized aspects of the practice of law, such as criminal defense attorneys or expensive corporate counsel, are also not inherently corrupt, greedy, unethical, immoral, etc. As you now observe, however, it certainly does raise issues of competing ethics and morality such as individual outcomes versus availability and fairness of process (i.e., the adversarial system)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:03:53-07:00","id":965779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965673#post965673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I should say so myself, I don't <i>believe</i> I would be a Seer, for ideological and religious reasons, and the fact that I am a very very devout Gnostic who would like any opressive gods to take their leave please, and <i>even </i>then I think I could probably see myself in a nice suit in Unity honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easy to say.<br /> <br /> But none of us have to cope with standing on the edge of obsession and realizing what the world being Unfathomable means. Faced with that, easy words suddenly become heavy. Sometimes, it's heavy enough to break the one thing that matters.<br /> <br /> No one thinks they're a Seer, and yet Seers are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:09:36-07:00","id":965784,"title":"","content":"Let me put it another way.<br /> <br /> Don't tell me you'd never steal food while you're sitting comfortably and well fed. I won't believe you.<br /> <br /> Don't tell me you won't when you're lost, scared, and desperate for the merest morsel, either. Show me, and for an instance, I'll believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:13:40-07:00","id":965786,"title":"","content":"Think they'd be more likely to kill me than recruit. I doubt anything could keep me from playing with the Abyss and they do frown on scelesti.<br /> <br /> They do have the Order of the Gate, though.<br /> <br /> I like this thread's title. It sounds like it would be an email subject passed around among Seer pylons.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's necessarily the best analogy, however. Joining the Seers takes commitment. Someone might steal food if they were starving, but would they learn to cook and get a job as a chef?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:13:46-07:00","id":965787,"title":"","content":"Y'know, I was thinking about the rungs in the ladder that Dave posted, and am now wondering about the implication that the SL isn't even at the top of it. The Oracles (And presumably other Ascended) are and archmasters are just a step below that. At the very least it means the SL believe themselves to be held accountable. At the most I think it means they would, by their own system, have to accept changes made to their beliefs and systems by these higher placed entities.<br /> <br /> Also, although regular Mages wouldn't likely know this, it doesn't really matter if the SL puts other supernaturals at the bottom of their ladder because IM lets us know they have their own sponsors which are unlikely to let them be crushed under the thumb of mere Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:43:25-07:00","id":966212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965787#post965787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, I was thinking about the rungs in the ladder that Dave posted, and am now wondering about the implication that the SL isn't even at the top of it. The Oracles (And presumably other Ascended) are and archmasters are just a step below that. At the very least it means the SL believe themselves to be held accountable. At the most I think it means they would, by their own system, have to accept changes made to their beliefs and systems by these higher placed entities.<br /> <br /> Also, although regular Mages wouldn't likely know this, it doesn't really matter if the SL puts other supernaturals at the bottom of their ladder because IM lets us know they have their own sponsors which are unlikely to let them be crushed under the thumb of mere Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Stewards of the Celestial Orrery are well aware of the Hiearchy and it is their sacred duty to make sure everyone else understand the ineffible will of the Oracles. :-)<br /> <br /> When I first got into this thread I would have been one of the first people to say, &quot;I'd never be a Seer of the Throne! It goes against every fiber of my being, every principle I hold dear! They'll have to kill me first!&quot; And I mean it. Use your Prime Sight ... It's the absolute Truth.<br /> <br /> Being recruited into the Seers of the Throne is more like a seduction than a pitch. They get you to share in some crime and once you're hooked, you can't wriggle free. And the rewards for service are so good that it would be easy for someone to become accustomed to them.<br /> <br /> Especially if you were trying to protect your family or provide for them. If you're a Seer and your superiors are using Profane Urim to speak to you through your wife and children, it might be very hard to do the right thing. Who's to say what the right thing is? If your superiors force your teenage daughter to attempt suicide and they warn you the next attempt won't fail, how can you refuse to follow orders. How many puppies will your drown or kitten will you light on fire to prevent your children from being suicided by your Seer superiors? To keep your wife faithful to you when she can be puppeteered into infidelity by the Profane Urim? And when you obey... new house, new car, college education paid for, trust funds for your kids, not a material concern in the world. You're the only one who knows. You're the only one who is suffering. But they're safe, and they're happy, and you're father of the year...<br /> <br /> &quot;I live only to serve and obey. Command me.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm happily married and we have five daughters.<br /> <br /> It's too easy to become a Seer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:41:33-07:00","id":966251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=966212#post966212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Stewards of the Celestial Orrery are well aware of the Hiearchy and it is their sacred duty to make sure everyone else understand the ineffible will of the Oracles. :-)<br /> <br /> When I first got into this thread I would have been one of the first people to say, &quot;I'd never be a Seer of the Throne! It goes against every fiber of my being, every principle I hold dear! They'll have to kill me first!&quot; And I mean it. Use your Prime Sight ... It's the absolute Truth.<br /> <br /> Being recruited into the Seers of the Throne is more like a seduction than a pitch. They get you to share in some crime and once you're hooked, you can't wriggle free. And the rewards for service are so good that it would be easy for someone to become accustomed to them.<br /> <br /> Especially if you were trying to protect your family or provide for them. If you're a Seer and your superiors are using Profane Urim to speak to you through your wife and children, it might be very hard to do the right thing. Who's to say what the right thing is? If your superiors force your teenage daughter to attempt suicide and they warn you the next attempt won't fail, how can you refuse to follow orders. How many puppies will your drown or kitten will you light on fire to prevent your children from being suicided by your Seer superiors? To keep your wife faithful to you when she can be puppeteered into infidelity by the Profane Urim? And when you obey... new house, new car, college education paid for, trust funds for your kids, not a material concern in the world. You're the only one who knows. You're the only one who is suffering. But they're safe, and they're happy, and you're father of the year...<br /> <br /> &quot;I live only to serve and obey. Command me.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm happily married and we have five daughters.<br /> <br /> It's too easy to become a Seer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. However, I would also note that most Seers are not devoted Prelates. The majority of Seers are toward the bottom of the Pyramid, and likely will not have to frequently perform &quot;questionable&quot; acts in service to the Order. The ethical costs for most Seers are relatively minor in the grand scheme of things, while the rewards are fantastic. For those who are truly ambitious and choose to attempt to climb the Pyramid hierarchy, while the obligations to the Exarchs may increase, the rewards, mundane and magical, are truly beyond compare. <br /> <br /> Look at what many people will tolerate in the real world for safety, security, comfort and wealth. When imagining the much darker CofD setting and the changes brought on by Awakening, to say nothing of the fact that the Exarchs are already actually in control and the Seers are the &quot;winning team,&quot; it's really not too difficult to understand why the Seers have no problems recruiting. The incentives are probably more than sufficient to recruit most of the time, with threats reserved for the very few recalcitrants who might know they have a choice and still resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:54:00-07:00","id":966612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=965625#post965625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) You do recognize the irony of &quot;Just accept I'm telling you the truth&quot; in this thread, right? Hell, on this specific topic even.<br /> <br /> 2) Funny how we're in different positions. I am over 20, have a high opinion of humanity and people in general* (AND I work in a call center, wrap your head around that), and I am also going off years of experience of seeing people commit their &quot;I would nevers&quot;. Fuck, I'm one of them.<br /> <br /> So, no. You keep believing you won't-that's how you avoid it-and I'll hope you can keep it.<br /> <br /> But I won't believe it.<br /> <br /> *And yes, this does still factor in I imagine a majority of people would be Seers if they Awakened. Even then, I believe in my species.</div> </div> </div> </div>I \u200btotally agree with the last line because it totally confirms my belief that the vast majority always take the easy way even if they know it's totally wrong. I'm not one of them. Money is cool but I need very little of it, food is nice but I go a couple days without it, friends and family I either have none or they're in no position to help me. With all of this as actual fact in my life I'm still comfortable. So If I had real power like a mage I would be doing all I could to help people find their best version of themselves not be some sellout toadies to the government (Exarchs).<br /> <br /> <br /> People by nature are liars, lazy, selfish, ignorant, fearful and easily mislead. So you better believe that he Seers have a leg up. Especially since both want nothing more then any mage can have with a modicum of effort for free.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-10-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:39:18-07:00","id":966634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=966612#post966612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I \u200btotally agree with the last line because it totally confirms my belief that the vast majority always take the easy way even if they know it's totally wrong. I'm not one of them. Money is cool but I need very little of it, food is nice but I go a couple days without it, friends and family I either have none or they're in no position to help me. With all of this as actual fact in my life I'm still comfortable. So If I had real power like a mage I would be doing all I could to help people find their best version of themselves not be some sellout toadies to the government (Exarchs).<br /> <br /> <br /> People by nature are liars, lazy, selfish, ignorant, fearful and easily mislead. So you better believe that he Seers have a leg up. Especially since both want nothing more then any mage can have with a modicum of effort for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then you are given an ultimatum. Serve the Exarchs, do the few tasks that they ask of you every now and then, and be allowed to help those you want on the side however much you want, or die. And take note that not only will you be killed, the people who you are most likely to want to help will be made to suffer for your refusal to cooperate. So you are given the choice to serve and help people, or die needlessly and condemn those you care to help to an increase in hardship and suffering.<br /> <br /> Would you bend a knee so that you might help people, even if occasionally you're asked to do something you might not normally want to do? The things asked of you probably aren't going to even be <i>that bad</i>. Deliver X to this address, retrieve Y from this location, convince Z to stop by at this time. Simple stuff. Or would you let your pride blind you, die a dogs death, and condemn those you wish to help?<br /> <br /> Which would you choose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:59:51-07:00","id":966643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=966612#post966612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I \u200btotally agree with the last line because it totally confirms my belief that the vast majority always take the easy way even if they know it's totally wrong. <b>I'm not one of them.</b> Money is cool but I need very little of it, food is nice but I go a couple days without it, friends and family I either have none or they're in no position to help me. With all of this as actual fact in my life I'm still comfortable. So If I had real power like a mage I would be doing all I could to help people find their best version of themselves not be some sellout toadies to the government (Exarchs).<br /> <br /> <br /> People by nature are liars, lazy, selfish, ignorant, fearful and easily mislead. So you better believe that he Seers have a leg up. Especially since both want nothing more then any mage can have with a modicum of effort for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put this in an Acanthusian perspective, since I speak that language.<br /> <br /> Always and Never are part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> For every promise made, there's an oath broken. There is always a world where the timing of circumstances collide and push a person into the time-space-perception they believed they would never be in. Hell, if you want to go whole hog and look at people from a non-linear, non-subjective point of view, every baby born will be, is, and always has been the End of the World and the Savior of the World and Everything In Between, and what the mage experiences is merely the shallow bit of reality he can experience due to the limits he works under as a being that labors under the Lie(Just because you wake up from the Lie does not mean you are free from it, and the notion that you are is one of the more sinister and subtle damnations that works itself through mage society and fan culture alike). You can't say <i>I won't</i> when <i>you already have</i>. An Acanthus has to accept that all people are all things, and their biggest tool is not to reject that but to embrace and master it and find the time and circumstances those aspects of their infinity are useful.<br /> <br /> Bringing it back down to earth, my problem with you trying to tell me <i>I won't</i> is that you just very simply <i>can't know that</i>. You have no idea where you'll be in your life, where you'll be thrown again and again, what time and tide'll do. In this particular case, none of us will never know because what we're talking about a fictional construct we'll never interact with-but where any of us are now, we cannot imagine what the bottom'll be like. I mean, it goes the other way too-you never know what heights you'll reach from where you are now either. But as it relates here, you'll never really know all the ways you can sell out until you've seen the payout on the days you really need it, where you <i>desperately want it</i>. Promises mean <i>jack shit </i>in the face of that. Denying it is useless-the only hope you have is working from &quot;I could&quot; and &quot;I might&quot; and deciding what to do from there.<br /> <br /> No one thinks they'll be a thief, a murderer, or a rapist, but people becomes thieves, murderers and rapists all the same.<br /> <br /> No one thinks they'll be a Seer, but the Seers <i>are</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>You'll never know until you are there</i>.<br /> <br /> You can tell yourself <i>I won't</i> all you like. If it helps you out, good for you.<br /> <br /> I don't believe it, and honestly, it seems like denying your potential to do or be something is to basically <i>not control it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-10-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:47:36-07:00","id":967092,"title":"","content":"I'm curious then what makes so many people /not/ Seers then? Realistically, I think most people would be Seers, certainly when I look out at the world we live in, I would say that if there were Seers, then right now, they'd be winning. <br /> <br /> It's hard to fight. Even for things you believe in. Either the Orders are populated by individuals so full of Hubris already that bending the knee, no matter how easy an beneficial to them, seems impossible, or there is a fire that is lit in the belly of some humans to reject the Lie and fight for truth no matter the cost. <br /> <br /> I think we all like to think that we love Truth above all, but I would bet that most people seriously offered the choice between a reality full of joy (that happens to be simulated) and real life with bills to pay and food to get, and emotional complications and all, would choose to get plugged in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:47:58-07:00","id":967129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967092#post967092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious then what makes so many people /not/ Seers then? Realistically, I think most people would be Seers, certainly when I look out at the world we live in, I would say that if there were Seers, then right now, they'd be winning.<br /> <br /> It's hard to fight. Even for things you believe in. Either the Orders are populated by individuals so full of Hubris already that bending the knee, no matter how easy an beneficial to them, seems impossible, or there is a fire that is lit in the belly of some humans to reject the Lie and fight for truth no matter the cost.<br /> <br /> I think we all like to think that we love Truth above all, but I would bet that most people seriously offered the choice between a reality full of joy (that happens to be simulated) and real life with bills to pay and food to get, and emotional complications and all, would choose to get plugged in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe general affiliation and Order membership often depends on little more than who first discovers and contacts a newly Awakened mage. Once you're in the Pentacle or Seers, it's not so easy to switch, either due to ingrained indoctrination or as a practical matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:36:44-07:00","id":967154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967092#post967092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious then what makes so many people /not/ Seers then? Realistically, I think most people would be Seers, certainly when I look out at the world we live in, I would say that if there were Seers, then right now, they'd be winning.<br /> <br /> It's hard to fight. Even for things you believe in. Either the Orders are populated by individuals so full of Hubris already that bending the knee, no matter how easy an beneficial to them, seems impossible, or there is a fire that is lit in the belly of some humans to reject the Lie and fight for truth no matter the cost.<br /> <br /> I think we all like to think that we love Truth above all, but I would bet that most people seriously offered the choice between a reality full of joy (that happens to be simulated) and real life with bills to pay and food to get, and emotional complications and all, would choose to get plugged in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all of us, i personally would join the seers sooo fast that i would knock the door of the old man on the house and back before he answered. I mean, power, money and hookers just for doing what i was about to with magic anyway? Just where do i sign up? Advance enough to get into one of those fake position with no upper mobility to make sure noone from upstairs attack me and then concentrate on the lower part of the pyramid and keeping my underlings down. And maybe one day....one day, have my own ministy.... the &quot;ministry of meh&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:59:23-07:00","id":967166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=966643#post966643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put this in an Acanthusian perspective, since I speak that language.<br /> <br /> Always and Never are part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> For every promise made, there's an oath broken. There is always a world where the timing of circumstances collide and push a person into the time-space-perception they believed they would never be in. Hell, if you want to go whole hog and look at people from a non-linear, non-subjective point of view, every baby born will be, is, and always has been the End of the World and the Savior of the World and Everything In Between, and what the mage experiences is merely the shallow bit of reality he can experience due to the limits he works under as a being that labors under the Lie(Just because you wake up from the Lie does not mean you are free from it, and the notion that you are is one of the more sinister and subtle damnations that works itself through mage society and fan culture alike). You can't say <i>I won't</i> when <i>you already have</i>. An Acanthus has to accept that all people are all things, and their biggest tool is not to reject that but to embrace and master it and find the time and circumstances those aspects of their infinity are useful.<br /> <br /> Bringing it back down to earth, my problem with you trying to tell me <i>I won't</i> is that you just very simply <i>can't know that</i>. You have no idea where you'll be in your life, where you'll be thrown again and again, what time and tide'll do. In this particular case, none of us will never know because what we're talking about a fictional construct we'll never interact with-but where any of us are now, we cannot imagine what the bottom'll be like. I mean, it goes the other way too-you never know what heights you'll reach from where you are now either. But as it relates here, you'll never really know all the ways you can sell out until you've seen the payout on the days you really need it, where you <i>desperately want it</i>. Promises mean <i>jack shit </i>in the face of that. Denying it is useless-the only hope you have is working from &quot;I could&quot; and &quot;I might&quot; and deciding what to do from there.<br /> <br /> No one thinks they'll be a thief, a murderer, or a rapist, but people becomes thieves, murderers and rapists all the same.<br /> <br /> No one thinks they'll be a Seer, but the Seers <i>are</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>You'll never know until you are there</i>.<br /> <br /> You can tell yourself <i>I won't</i> all you like. If it helps you out, good for you.<br /> <br /> I don't believe it, and honestly, it seems like denying your potential to do or be something is to basically <i>not control it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I still think that if I was Awakened, I would take one look at the Seers and decide they are in desperate need of a cosmic wedgie. To me, they are the culmination of every &quot;person in position of power who is screwing the little guy to stay on top&quot; stereotype I've ever seen, and then takes it even further. Seriously, if I was a Kindred, I could kind of understand where the Invictus are coming from, or at least grudgingly accept them as a necessary part of the equation. The Seers, on the other hand, just use their power for their own betterment and pleasure, and too often that seems to boil down to kicking puppies to hear the yelps of pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:06:58-07:00","id":967171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967166#post967166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I still think that if I was Awakened, I would take one look at the Seers and decide they are in desperate need of a cosmic wedgie. To me, they are the culmination of every &quot;person in position of power who is screwing the little guy to stay on top&quot; stereotype I've ever seen, and then takes it even further. Seriously, if I was a Kindred, I could kind of understand where the Invictus are coming from, or at least grudgingly accept them as a necessary part of the equation. The Seers, on the other hand, just use their power for their own betterment and pleasure, and too often that seems to boil down to kicking puppies to hear the yelps of pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I suggest you read up on your Seers again. The Tyranny of the Defeated is not so simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:13:19-07:00","id":967172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967166#post967166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I still think that if I was Awakened, I would take one look at the Seers and decide they are in desperate need of a cosmic wedgie. To me, they are the culmination of every &quot;person in position of power who is screwing the little guy to stay on top&quot; stereotype I've ever seen, and then takes it even further. Seriously, if I was a Kindred, I could kind of understand where the Invictus are coming from, or at least grudgingly accept them as a necessary part of the equation. The Seers, on the other hand, just use their power for their own betterment and pleasure, and too often that seems to boil down to kicking puppies to hear the yelps of pain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most newly Awakened mages don't know the full extent of Mage society or the depth of Seers oppression. It's not like you're handed a copy of Mage: The Awakening after you sign your name on the Watchtower.<br /> <br /> If you're first introduced to Seers when you Awaken, they look damn good. A society of fellow mages providing safety and training, with the added benefit of significant magical resources and a life of resplendent luxury. The awful demands and/or threats don't come until later, and by then you just might not care and certainly can't get out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-11-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:52:55-07:00","id":967190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=966634#post966634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then you are given an ultimatum. Serve the Exarchs, do the few tasks that they ask of you every now and then, and be allowed to help those you want on the side however much you want, or die. And take note that not only will you be killed, the people who you are most likely to want to help will be made to suffer for your refusal to cooperate. So you are given the choice to serve and help people, or die needlessly and condemn those you care to help to an increase in hardship and suffering.<br /> <br /> Would you bend a knee so that you might help people, even if occasionally you're asked to do something you might not normally want to do? The things asked of you probably aren't going to even be <i>that bad</i>. Deliver X to this address, retrieve Y from this location, convince Z to stop by at this time. Simple stuff. Or would you let your pride blind you, die a dogs death, and condemn those you wish to help?<br /> <br /> Which would you choose?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have already faced this choice many times in IRL already so it's laughably easy. Bring it on and do your best. See as an Obrimos I basically know without a doubt there is a Supreme Being that runs The Show. My sleeper faith actually proven right before my eyes. Simple stuff. It's what every Christian deals with daily and it's right there in front and center in back and white (or red for Jesus's words) for the less then faithful, knowledgeable or newer Christians. It really is that simple. Help people do not screw them over ever. Especially to your advantage. You can educate and put them in bad situations as an object lesson for personal improvement. BUT YOU DON'T TAKE ADVANTAGE FOR ADVANCEMENT OR ADVANTAGE'S SAKE. It's just not a realistic choice to me IRL or as a Mage. It's part of the reason I understand and mostly agree with anyone that isn't The Seers.<br /> <br /> When you get to see behind the curtain by you own eyes the Seer's requirement pitch isn't some easy slam dunk as described by so many on this thread. It's not like you just awaken with no path like Mage the Ascension you awaken to a certain way of seeing things beyond personal belief and know it has validity and you know you can already achieve what the Seers offer if you don't panic and sit down and think about what your real options are then choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-11-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T23:17:49-07:00","id":967197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967129#post967129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe general affiliation and Order membership often depends on little more than who first discovers and contacts a newly Awakened mage. Once you're in the Pentacle or Seers, it's not so easy to switch, either due to ingrained indoctrination or as a practical matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally disagree even though you have awakened you still have every bias, belief, faith system (atheist included) you had as a sleeper. It's why the GotV willingly shuttle off newly awakened mages to the order that fits them best. Seers won't force a choice right on the spot because they're all about seduction and seduction doesn't work on the unwilling.\u200b It isn't like any mage from the start can't have comfort and security so that is a dumb promise.... hit my friends and family? Well that's an asshole move so now I'm totally wondering about your actual motives and in full assessment mode. I didn't do anything to you and your's so why the threats? Jus\u200bt leaves me wondering just what is your actual angle. Remember the Seers are the minority for good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-11-2016, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T01:40:29-07:00","id":967237,"title":"","content":"I would say that the relatively low Seer numbers may at least partially be that way because of the same reason only a specific type of obsessive personality can Awaken. The <i>kind</i> of person that Awakens does definitely not have the typical human's attitude towards reality. And these obsessive people, especially after Awakening as mages, can be *really* stubborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-11-2016, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T04:47:08-07:00","id":967261,"title":"","content":"Back to the original topic - the clip provided does not support the subject (Why Silver Ladder should never fulfill their dreams). If anything, it should be <b>&quot;Why morons would not last very long as Arch-Masters&quot;.</b> In the CoD universe, this person would violate the Pax Arcanum in a Severe manner. Such blatant ignorance would surely bring down swift and terrible judgement because he is a dangerous individual who wields his power without thought to the consequences of his actions.<br /> <br /> I don't get the hate for the Silver Ladder, but I think that the previous corebook failed to succeed pitching the Order to players. Personally, I get edgy when faced with a &quot;class&quot; that implies leadership for simple virtue of picking a class (much like I am leary of the Leadership feat dictating control of the tabletop group in Pathfinder). I have also encountered a few people who misinterpret (or completely ignore) the core principles of the Elemental Precepts and the Lex Magica, believing they have carte blanche to play the &quot;wannabe vampire/mobster tyrant prince&quot; or &quot;white-hat Seer&quot; without answering to the tenets of the Order. And then there is the Nemean, the worst advertisement for the Ladder and an obvious reinforcement of a negative stereotype.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1605-thatguy","name":"ThatGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T05:00:30-07:00","id":967269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967261#post967261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have also encountered a few people who misinterpret (or completely ignore) the core principles of the Elemental Precepts and the Lex Magica, believing they have carte blanche to play the &quot;wannabe vampire/mobster tyrant prince&quot; or &quot;white-hat Seer&quot; without answering to the tenets of the Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, those players made the same mistakes some in universe thearchs make. This shows that definitely at least <i>something</i> in the SL book was done right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:06:34-07:00","id":967292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967190#post967190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have already faced this choice many times in IRL already so it's laughably easy. Bring it on and do your best. See as an Obrimos I basically know without a doubt there is a Supreme Being that runs The Show. My sleeper faith actually proven right before my eyes. Simple stuff. It's what every Christian deals with daily and it's right there in front and center in back and white (or red for Jesus's words) for the less then faithful, knowledgeable or newer Christians. It really is that simple. Help people do not screw them over ever. Especially to your advantage. You can educate and put them in bad situations as an object lesson for personal improvement. BUT YOU DON'T TAKE ADVANTAGE FOR ADVANCEMENT OR ADVANTAGE'S SAKE. It's just not a realistic choice to me IRL or as a Mage. It's part of the reason I understand and mostly agree with anyone that isn't The Seers.<br /> <br /> When you get to see behind the curtain by you own eyes the Seer's requirement pitch isn't some easy slam dunk as described by so many on this thread. It's not like you just awaken with no path like Mage the Ascension you awaken to a certain way of seeing things beyond personal belief and know it has validity and you know you can already achieve what the Seers offer if you don't panic and sit down and think about what your real options are then choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with what Kumiko says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:40:02-07:00","id":967299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967292#post967292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with what Kumiko says.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you just say how easy it would be to coerce you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:50:09-07:00","id":967306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967299#post967299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't you just say how easy it would be to coerce you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like he just... got coerced... by Kumiko. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />(Yeaaah!!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-11-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:08:50-07:00","id":967546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967190#post967190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you get to see behind the curtain by you own eyes the Seer's requirement pitch isn't some easy slam dunk as described by so many on this thread. It's not like you just awaken with no path like Mage the Ascension you awaken to a certain way of seeing things beyond personal belief and know it has validity and you know you can already achieve what the Seers offer if you don't panic and sit down and think about what your real options are then choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>But who says you get the luxury of sitting down and thinking about your real options? If you're standing there with the proverbial (or literal!) gun to your head you simply don't have the option to sit and think about it. You can bend a knee now and survive to think about it and possibly try to defect later (which might end just as badly for you), or you could reject the offer, die, and then they'll use you as an example to others in the same situation about what happens to the people who snub their noses at Seer generosity, and thus serve their purposes in death in a way that you were unwilling to do in life.<br /> <br /> If the Seers are the first to find you then chances are you're going to bend a knee, if only for a while, or die. I mean the choice is yours (usually, sometimes they might just mind fuck you and take away that choice altogether), but for most people there isn't really much of a choice to make. Regardless, the Seers will usually get theirs one way or another, be it paid in service or blood.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying it's hopeless, and that you automatically will serve them, but there are definitely situations where you could be forced to be a Seer regardless of what you might want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-11-2016, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:20:38-07:00","id":967589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967546#post967546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying it's hopeless, and that you automatically will serve them, but there are definitely situations where you could be forced to be a Seer regardless of what you might want.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also can be repeated enough - life for most Seers is really pretty darn good. Low and mid tier/pyramid Seers have lives of luxury and excess, tremendous magical and mundane resources, political, economic and social power, and the ability to pursue their own interests most of the time, and all for the low, low price of an occasional errand for actual gods who already won the war to control reality. A lot of people do much worse for a lot less in real life. We all make compromises for safety, security and material comforts. I believe the threats for noncompliance are rarely necessary. <br /> <br /> The Seers are evil and I hope I would never join. However, the temptations and risks are so very easy to understand.<br /> <br /> Lastly, despite the rhetoric, Pentacle mages are quite often anything but paragons of virtue, charity and generosity, and that's before any consideration of what most any mage will due in pursuit of an Obsession. <br /> <br /> If you're going to single-mindedly use your new cosmic powers for your own benefit and purposes, as most mages will do, you might as well have the best toys, drugs and hookers... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:36:06-07:00","id":967597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967589#post967589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also can be repeated enough - life for most Seers is really pretty darn good. Low and mid tier/pyramid Seers have lives of luxury and excess, tremendous magical and mundane resources, political, economic and social power, and the ability to pursue their own interests most of the time, and all for the low, low price of an occasional errand for actual gods who already won the war to control reality. A lot of people do much worse for a lot less in real life. We all make compromises for safety, security and material comforts. I believe the threats for noncompliance are rarely necessary.<br /> <br /> The Seers are evil and I hope I would never join. However, the temptations and risks are so very easy to understand.<br /> <br /> Lastly, despite the rhetoric, Pentacle mages are quite often anything but paragons of virtue, charity and generosity, and that's before any consideration of what most any mage will due in pursuit of an Obsession.<br /> <br /> If you're going to single-mindedly use your new cosmic powers for your own benefit and purposes, as most mages will do, you might as well have the best toys, drugs and hookers... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And I completely agree, but if you are dead set upon not joining them, or worse, joining some opposing faction, they are definitely not above just killing you before you can become a nuisance. They will without a doubt try to bribe you over to their side, be it by lies or simply giving you what you want most for the price of servitude, but failing that, a good old threat of bodily harm isn't something they'd shy away from. I think it was in the Chicago book that it mentioned how the Seers in that city would pick up newly awakened and give them a ride in a limo, where they would then give them their recruitment speech. If they accepted, all the better, but if they refused, then that would be the last ride the person ever had and then it became a ride to go to a spot where they dumped the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:11:28-07:00","id":967615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967597#post967597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I completely agree, but if you are dead set upon not joining them, or worse, joining some opposing faction, they are definitely not above just killing you before you can become a nuisance. They will without a doubt try to bribe you over to their side, be it by lies or simply giving you what you want most for the price of servitude, but failing that, a good old threat of bodily harm isn't something they'd shy away from. I think it was in the Chicago book that it mentioned how the Seers in that city would pick up newly awakened and give them a ride in a limo, where they would then give them their recruitment speech. If they accepted, all the better, but if they refused, then that would be the last ride the person ever had and then it became a ride to go to a spot where they dumped the body.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Seers definitely have very enticing carrots and deadly sticks as part of their recruitment pitch.<br /> <br /> If offered the choice of wealth beyond avarice, great power and the very best toys, or pain and death for you and your loved ones, well..., the answer would be pretty clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T22:38:46-07:00","id":967789,"title":"","content":"I wanna throw my voice in and say that I'm not so sure the Seers would ever use (direct) threats in their recruiting. They might kill people who reject the offer, sure, and use threats once they've signed up, but threatening someone is a terrible way to ensure the kind of loyalty needed to make sure they don't jump ship at the absolute first opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:13:08-07:00","id":968028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967299#post967299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't you just say how easy it would be to coerce you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But imagine if I had permission to do the right thing from my wife and daughters? No force on Earth could stop me.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T05:41:07-07:00","id":969836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=963609#post963609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limited human minds cannot predict every possible results - it's also fundament of Wisdom-as-Trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't.<br /> <br /> If I go out to the store this morning to pick up some eggs, and I have a choice of routes, and I pick one, and then on the way a drunk staggers out from behind a blind corner into the path of my car before I can slow down, that is a consequence of my choice - my choice to turn right instead of left or whatever - and of my inability to foresee the future and the outcome of all possible circumstances. It has jack to do with my Wisdom, however.<br /> <br /> Holding people culpable for the outcomes of actions taken in good faith and without impossible knowledge of the circumstances elevates absurdity to the level of an art form. Under that rubric, every postman who unknowingly delivered a mail bomb, or a ransom note, or a Publisher's Sweepstakes scam, would be some kind of criminal.<br /> <br /> Wisdom is not some absolute measure of how much harm you have unknowingly - or even knowingly! - caused. It is not an evilometer. What it does do is indicate the degree of care a character takes in their choices out of their feeling of connection to others - how likely they are to see themselves and their goals as the only worthwhile end. Going back to my first example, if I hit the man because I was speeding, because I figured that my precious time was way more important than the law or other people's safety, *that* would be a strike against Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:36:39-07:00","id":969858,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12136\" data-vbnamecard=\"12136\">jacobkosh</a> - And then we take our 'Awakened cop' example that characters of good intentions are hit hard by Wisdom-As-Trait. Then you can say that Silver Ladder, for making every one live in Paradise, would get lowest Wisdom dice pool, as they do not try make anything work under now governing principles of CoD universe.<br /> <br /> Not too mention lower penalties from planned murder than crime of passion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:02:43-07:00","id":969875,"title":"","content":"Old conversation, and I see you still don't understand Wisdom <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:17:12-07:00","id":969880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=969858#post969858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12136_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12136\" data-vbnamecard=\"12136\">jacobkosh</a> - And then we take our 'Awakened cop' example that characters of good intentions are hit hard by Wisdom-As-Trait. Then you can say that Silver Ladder, for making every one live in Paradise, would get lowest Wisdom dice pool, as they do not try make anything work under now governing principles of CoD universe.<br /> <br /> Not too mention lower penalties from planned murder than crime of passion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Naw.<br /> <br /> The opposite of Wisdom is Obsession, not action, and the best way to conserve Wisdom is not to just offer a teenage, fatalistic shrug and accept every status quo that is presented to you - that's just another path to alienation from your fellow human beings, another path to detachment (in this case, detachment from the struggles and sufferings of the people around you).<br /> <br /> Every mage has an obsession and every order has its own path to Hubris. An Arrow's preoccupation with self-perfection and endless struggle is no less of a potential pitfall than a Ladder's revolutionary zeal: the danger to Wisdom is in the act of Obsessing, but Wisdom isn't a proxy measure for whether the object of Obsession itself is good, bad, or indifferent. These things are decoupled. Self-knowledge and self-improvement are generally regarded as positive goals - it's certainly hard to construct an ethical schema where they're explicitly and always anti-good! - but low-Wisdom Arrows exist. Domination and enslavement are almost unquestionably bad things but high-wisdom Seers exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:46:53-07:00","id":969897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=969836#post969836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I go out to the store this morning to pick up some eggs, and I have a choice of routes, and I pick one, and then on the way a drunk staggers out from behind a blind corner into the path of my car before I can slow down, that is a consequence of my choice - my choice to turn right instead of left or whatever - and of my inability to foresee the future and the outcome of all possible circumstances. It has jack to do with my Wisdom, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to play with this idea for a moment here, the Awakened frequently <i>do</i> have the ability to foresee the future. Does an Acanthus who, just going about their morning routine, drives into the same drunk face a Wisdom strike if they didn't divine the possibility? Does a more powerful Acanthus face a Wisdom strike if they <i>don't</i> use their magic to rewind time a little and slam on the brakes sooner?<br /> <br /> Is a choice where you refuse to take maximum precaution still an &quot;innocent&quot; one? How powerful does an Awakened have to become before, like the God defied by the Problem of Evil, their lack of action crosses over into negligence? If Wisdom is about the degree of care a character exercises in their choices, how safe are they expected to make their decisions to avoid Hubris? Is it sufficient just to consider the person you act on immediately, or like the Great Law of the Iroquois, must you consider it down unto the seventh generation? Is there a difference in the level of consideration expected based on the power of the Awakened?<br /> <br /> These are the questions that keep thearchs up at night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:28:09-07:00","id":969930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=969897#post969897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to play with this idea for a moment here, the Awakened frequently <i>do</i> have the ability to foresee the future. Does an Acanthus who, just going about their morning routine, drives into the same drunk face a Wisdom strike if they didn't divine the possibility? Does a more powerful Acanthus face a Wisdom strike if they <i>don't</i> use their magic to rewind time a little and slam on the brakes sooner?<br /> <br /> Is a choice where you refuse to take maximum precaution still an &quot;innocent&quot; one? How powerful does an Awakened have to become before, like the God defied by the Problem of Evil, their lack of action crosses over into negligence? If Wisdom is about the degree of care a character exercises in their choices, how safe are they expected to make their decisions to avoid Hubris? Is it sufficient just to consider the person you act on immediately, or like the Great Law of the Iroquois, must you consider it down unto the seventh generation? Is there a difference in the level of consideration expected based on the power of the Awakened?<br /> <br /> These are the questions that keep thearchs up at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to consider Wisdom as separate from ethics or morality inasmuch as it's explicitly measuring how likely you are to use magic as a shortcut, and how that separates you from mundane humans. Taking it strictly as written, Wisdom doesn't have any sins for failure to use magic. Early on, the Arcana are not innate to a mage's selfhood - he will still think of himself as a regular person - and later on, at higher Gnosis, it reflects that magic isn't a passive choice but an active one that carries its own risks that may outweigh the consequences of not using it.<br /> <br /> A freshly-minted Acanthus, for instance, just out of Acanthus High and still getting a grip on even the basics of his arcana, might not realize that he could have done something to suggest the better route to take...but that's not going to stop him feeling horrible or guilty about it when it happens. Conversely, an experienced enchanter who has seen a lot of people's Fates fulfilled or cut short might have a somewhat inhuman sangfroid about the death of one person but would feel terrible about their sloppy Fatesmanship in letting it happen in the first place.<br /> <br /> The second guy is probably more culpable morally, but I wouldn't rule that he had committed an Act of Hubris. He probably does have a lower Wisdom score in general, though, which is reflected in his detached outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:15:19-07:00","id":970097,"title":"","content":"I think this is where we run into a problem, since murder is a Wisdom sin, even when done without magic; that certain magic acts are sins when they could be accomplished no other way; that a callousness to one's fellow human beings is not a trait exclusive to magicians.<br /> <br /> It feels to me that any claim that Wisdom isn't tied to morals and ethics will run against the problem that it clearly, say, values human lives and souls over the lives of plants and animals. It claims to value self-control, but self-control of a very specific type.<br /> <br /> Wisdom seems to cleave to a very modern humanistic and libertarian view of what is a &quot;normal&quot; human, and values that humanity above all else. It is not, by any means, a schema that'd have been accepted universally before the rise of modernity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:07:03-07:00","id":970137,"title":"","content":"That's just what the authors put down to give you some sort of idea of how Wisdom can be structured. The book actively encourages you to change up and customize the list as you deem appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:11:41-07:00","id":970144,"title":"","content":"Not really the point; that magic-free acts at all can cause a Wisdom break brings the idea that it's about magic into question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:13:32-07:00","id":970147,"title":"","content":"Only if you keep magic free acts in your schema of Wisdom guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T23:32:30-07:00","id":971182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=967546#post967546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But who says you get the luxury of sitting down and thinking about your real options? If you're standing there with the proverbial (or literal!) gun to your head you simply don't have the option to sit and think about it. You can bend a knee now and survive to think about it and possibly try to defect later (which might end just as badly for you), or you could reject the offer, die, and then they'll use you as an example to others in the same situation about what happens to the people who snub their noses at Seer generosity, and thus serve their purposes in death in a way that you were unwilling to do in life.<br /> <br /> If the Seers are the first to find you then chances are you're going to bend a knee, if only for a while, or die. I mean the choice is yours (usually, sometimes they might just mind fuck you and take away that choice altogether), but for most people there isn't really much of a choice to make. Regardless, the Seers will usually get theirs one way or another, be it paid in service or blood.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying it's hopeless, and that you automatically will serve them, but there are definitely situations where you could be forced to be a Seer regardless of what you might want.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seers and direct? No honey that isn't how they work. Remember what they offer is attainable with a modicum of work. Threats are stupid and threats to me or my family makes you a serious enemy and just let's me prepare and confirm what an asshole you really are. This just life experience guys I'm not a hater but I know when people are playing me behind the fake smiles. It just don't play that game for previous reasons and more. If I were a mage I'd get mad and strike back at such crap and probably more. I hate social justice and anything related because they have no clue about me and my beliefs or disabilities. So they should sit down, shut up and learn from someone that lives it 24/7 like myself. If I had real power I would never be tempted by temporal things. And that is the whole game the Seers are about and offer. I already have that as a mundane disabled woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-17-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T23:58:53-07:00","id":971189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971182#post971182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Seers and direct? No honey that isn't how they work. Remember what they offer is attainable with a modicum of work. Threats are stupid and threats to me or my family makes you a serious enemy and just let's me prepare and confirm what an asshole you really are. This just life experience guys I'm not a hater but I know when people are playing me behind the fake smiles. It just don't play that game for previous reasons and more. If I were a mage I'd get mad and strike back at such crap and probably more. I hate social justice and anything related because they have no clue about me and my beliefs or disabilities. So they should sit down, shut up and learn from someone that lives it 24/7 like myself. If I had real power I would never be tempted by temporal things. And that is the whole game the Seers are about and offer. I already have that as a mundane disabled woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seers can and will go with any route that will work, and threat of violence is a perfectly viable course of action. And as a new mage, the simple fact of the matter is that they're going to have you hilariously outgunned. They'll have more resources, experience, power (both magical and influential), and hold pretty much every other advantage imaginable over you. So again, telling them to sit down and shut up is just asking for a quick ticket to a shallow grave. That said, assuming they don't care enough to make threats they, again, might just skip straight to the killing part if turned down, after all, if you aren't with them, then chances are you're against them, and it's almost certainly better to quietly deal with the problem now than when it becomes a bigger issue. <br /> <br /> That said, if you stick to your guns even knowing you're pretty much killing yourself doing so then more power to you I guess. That's respectable in a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T00:10:06-07:00","id":971191,"title":"","content":"Guys, while I do disagree with Kumiko's reasoning of why she'd never join, I gotta say the angle you're taking is both cartoonish and untrue to the Seers portrayal. Remember that at the heart of it all the Seers main thrust is that everyone <i>fails, </i>that everyone <i>will always fail</i>, and that the best thing that can happen is to make &quot;second place&quot; a comfortable thing. The Seers aren't merely powerful, they are powerful in their <i>defeat</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-17-2016, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T00:37:16-07:00","id":971193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971191#post971191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, while I do disagree with Kumiko's reasoning of why she'd never join, I gotta say the angle you're taking is both cartoonish and untrue to the Seers portrayal. Remember that at the heart of it all the Seers main thrust is that everyone <i>fails, </i>that everyone <i>will always fail</i>, and that the best thing that can happen is to make &quot;second place&quot; a comfortable thing. The Seers aren't merely powerful, they are powerful in their <i>defeat</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct and I agree with. Hint for everyone I already live what they offer. To them I am a failure but in reality I'm not because my personal standards of success are way beyond what any Seer could or would offer me. Unlike a Silver Ladder or even a the Free Council.\u200b Guns? Directly threatening me? Come on. Healing me on the spot like Jesus.... now you have my attention at least. Do that and bring my family back from the dead..... interesting. Got anymore tricks?<br /> <br /> Life has taught me there are two things in life I can trust. Myself and God. And usually myself screws up. I would be obrimos. Just sit back and think about that and my previous posts if I were a mage... think hard and carefully.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-17-2016, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T00:42:38-07:00","id":971194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971193#post971193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is correct and I agree with. Hint for everyone I already live what they offer. To them I am a failure but in reality I'm not because my personal standards of success are way beyond what any Seer could or would offer me. Unlike a Silver Ladder or even a the Free Council.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you don't, because you neither have metaphysical hunger for the transformative actualization of becoming one with shadows of higher truths that literally warp your entire presence, nor do you have a concept-will-god directly tapped into your soul giving you the fast track to said actualization.<br /> <br /> The prize of the Seers is not the money, power, or fame-those are trappings. The actual prize is the Exarchs doing all the stuff that makes you a Mage for you while you put yourself in the right place, time, and frame of mind for them. The actual prize is Feeding Your Obsessions without Doing The Work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T01:04:52-07:00","id":971196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971194#post971194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you don't, because you neither have metaphysical hunger for the transformative actualization of becoming one with shadows of higher truths that literally warp your entire presence, nor do you have a concept-will-god directly tapped into your soul giving you the fast track to said actualization.<br /> <br /> The prize of the Seers is not the money, power, or fame-those are trappings. The actual prize is the Exarchs doing all the stuff that makes you a Mage for you while you put yourself in the right place, time, and frame of mind for them. The actual prize is Feeding Your Obsessions without Doing The Work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I prefer doing my achievements myself. Just ask anyone that knows me. And with God's help it's worked just fine for more years than you might guess.<br /> <br /> I like you by the way would you mind PMing me? I think we could be friends.\u200bI like that you're intelligent and you're not closed minded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-17-2016, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:04:36-07:00","id":971323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971191#post971191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, while I do disagree with Kumiko's reasoning of why she'd never join, I gotta say the angle you're taking is both cartoonish and untrue to the Seers portrayal. Remember that at the heart of it all the Seers main thrust is that everyone <i>fails, </i>that everyone <i>will always fail</i>, and that the best thing that can happen is to make &quot;second place&quot; a comfortable thing. The Seers aren't merely powerful, they are powerful in their <i>defeat</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kumiko said in no situation, right? So I'm going with a bad but not quite worst case scenario. A situation that isn't going to <i>always </i>apply with every group of Seers one might find themselves face to face with but a type that isn't going to be <i>that</i> rare. So assuming Kumiko is a situation where she gets found by a group of Seers who operate similar to the Executive Suite from Chicago. At which point, assuming she can read the situation as well as she portrays herself able to, will find herself in a situation where it's join or die. I'll admit it probably won't be said outright but it is totally a join or die situation.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I don't think it's <i>that</i> likely to be able to that easily divine their intentions. After just coming down from the high of awakening you're met by people who are willing to take you under their wing, provide you with wealth beyond imagination and the knowledge/teaching necessary to master/understand this new facet of reality you've stumbled upon. Assuming you're thinking clear enough to notice any traces of bullshit, and sharp enough to realize how deep you the water you're swimming in actually is and that those fins sticking out of the water don't belong to a bunch of helpful dolphins, what can you really do in such a situation? You don't know about the Pentacle, so as while you might suspect that there <i>might</i> be a rivaling faction <i>somewhere</i> you have no idea where they are, what their ideals are, or whether they're going to be any better (Kinda? But just as bad in a lot of aspects?). <br /> <br /> So in a situation of join or die, what do? Keep in mind I'm talking newly awakened here too, you'd only be rocking like 1 dot worth of instinctive understanding in both of your ruling arcana and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:07:11-07:00","id":971370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971323#post971323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kumiko said in no situation, right? So I'm going with a bad but not quite worst case scenario. A situation that isn't going to <i>always </i>apply with every group of Seers one might find themselves face to face with but a type that isn't going to be <i>that</i> rare. So assuming Kumiko is a situation where she gets found by a group of Seers who operate similar to the Executive Suite from Chicago. At which point, assuming she can read the situation as well as she portrays herself able to, will find herself in a situation where it's join or die. I'll admit it probably won't be said outright but it is totally a join or die situation.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I don't think it's <i>that</i> likely to be able to that easily divine their intentions. After just coming down from the high of awakening you're met by people who are willing to take you under their wing, provide you with wealth beyond imagination and the knowledge/teaching necessary to master/understand this new facet of reality you've stumbled upon. Assuming you're thinking clear enough to notice any traces of bullshit, and sharp enough to realize how deep you the water you're swimming in actually is and that those fins sticking out of the water don't belong to a bunch of helpful dolphins, what can you really do in such a situation? You don't know about the Pentacle, so as while you might suspect that there <i>might</i> be a rivaling faction <i>somewhere</i> you have no idea where they are, what their ideals are, or whether they're going to be any better (Kinda? But just as bad in a lot of aspects?).<br /> <br /> So in a situation of join or die, what do? Keep in mind I'm talking newly awakened here too, you'd only be rocking like 1 dot worth of instinctive understanding in both of your ruling arcana and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it's not a convincing argument in this situation.<br /> <br /> Let me go to a similar case I used in Changeling for some clarification-A Huntsman grabs a newly returned changeling, drags them to the edge of Arcadia, and gives them a choice: Help us or go back. In this scenario, there's a widely understood and oft-accepted premise that Arcadia is The Worst Thing Ever to changelings. Dying is kinder than Arcadia. It is not implausible, hanging on the edge of <i>that</i> cliff, a changeling would be willing to compromise their beliefs and betray their friends, families, and beliefs.<br /> <br /> Now, mind you, that's still kind of cartoonish and not really how the Huntsmen work. They do use scare tactics, but they play a complex game beyond that, taking advantage of the fluid nature of the fae perspective in all it's forms in order to foster distrust in one's self and others and them in you and ideally try to influence a changeling to change their mind on deep, fundamental levels so that even a partial success yields long standing results. But it works because of the premise that we can accept in the comfort of our homes, because we have, for the most part, bought into the books.<br /> <br /> Mage though? Mage doesn't have exterior circumstances like this. This is not a game heavily about the impact of outside influences and how one shifts from one view to another, this is a game about the failures and triumphs of the human will, that change is fundamentally at the hands of the person confronted with it. So we as players, looking in, just see a classic scenario we have seen in media countless times with no real personal experience for why they would say &quot;Sure, I'll join.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, intellectually we know that the stress and the fear and the confusion and the anger and the <i>everything</i> going on at the time might sway us one way or another, but we've also been trained to know the answer is NO in that scenario, that principles are worth dying for and important and generally we've just seen enough shit that portrays saying &quot;I choose death&quot; in a positive light. And from the comfort of our own homes, secure in our knowledge and faith and feelings and bathrobes, it's easy to say &quot;I wouldn't join.&quot; And so when you're trying to convince someone that they might, of course they're going to say no. It's not compelling. It's not an invasive scenario, it doesn't subvert or challenge one's conventional understandings. People <i>know</i> to say No to that. They know to say No to the guy trying to buy you.<br /> <br /> If there is an appeal to make, It is not through blatant displays of force, it's through subtle and insidious manipulations of that which a person takes pride in. The Seers aren't going to put a gun to your head, they're going to find ways to make you question yourself, what you stand for. They will find the cracks in your armor and they will take advantage of that with velvet gloves. Sure, they'll keep up exterior pressure, but they aren't going to compromise the entire's organization as the soft second place.<br /> <br /> If the Seers try to win someone over, the first thing they are always going to do is get someone to <i>give up</i>. Completely on their own accord.<br /> <br /> And, you know, it's hard for anyone to know just <i>how</i> they would give up. The worlds we live in seem very sure to us-they are designed that way, and we are programmed to make it easy to find, because otherwise we'd be gibbering balls of neuroses on overload. These things seem safe and solid to us, and it takes a lot to make them ephemeral. If you told me five years ago that I would be planning on leaving the Mormon Church, I'd have laughed at you. It now seems inevitable to me, but then, it was inconceivable, and that's with me having been aware of a majority of the things that did, in fact, go and play into why I finally got tired of the bullshit.<br /> <br /> And this is half of why my point is <i>you won't know until you're there</i>, because it's inconceivable to see that which is firm around us fade away into smoke. This is why I generally do not posit why Kumiko specifically would. It's a personal affair.<br /> <br /> (The other half of the point is that saying &quot;i wouldn't&quot; basically reads to me as &quot;I'm not examining with myself with a critical eye, looking for weaknesses, and shoring up against them, so by all means go for it&quot;, and further stills that those flaws are perceived as possibly not having a place in the Way Things Are and something that needs to be accepted for one's long term transcendence.)<br /> <br /> And strictly speaking, it's also, from an in-universe perspective, not very practical for the Seers to go around doing the &quot;Gun to Head&quot; conversion trick. You might win a temporary ally, but you have also laid the seeds of future shit-kicking going down. The Seers might be a contentious bunch, fighting each other over positions and such, but they still wouldn't want to essentially hire someone in a way that invites them to set them up the bomb at the worst possible time.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, no, if you want to try and open someone to the possibility of them joining the bad guys, don't go with a classical black and white scene we've all seen and know the answer to. Argue from a position that is chartreuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:09:56-07:00","id":971372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971196#post971196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. I prefer doing my achievements myself. Just ask anyone that knows me. And with God's help it's worked just fine for more years than you might guess.<br /> <br /> I like you by the way would you mind PMing me? I think we could be friends.\u200bI like that you're intelligent and you're not closed minded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure, I'll do that after this.<br /> <br /> And cool, I'm for that. I get that. My point is that that might not always be the case, and that I feel the best way of ensuring it stays that way is to explore all the ways you might not stay in that place and put your guards on that.<br /> <br /> Know Thyself is key to any form of integrity, and it is a very bittersweet thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:29:45-07:00","id":971387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971370#post971370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that it's not a convincing argument in this situation.<br /> <br /> Let me go to a similar case I used in Changeling for some clarification-A Huntsman grabs a newly returned changeling, drags them to the edge of Arcadia, and gives them a choice: Help us or go back. In this scenario, there's a widely understood and oft-accepted premise that Arcadia is The Worst Thing Ever to changelings. Dying is kinder than Arcadia. It is not implausible, hanging on the edge of <i>that</i> cliff, a changeling would be willing to compromise their beliefs and betray their friends, families, and beliefs.<br /> <br /> Now, mind you, that's still kind of cartoonish and not really how the Huntsmen work. They do use scare tactics, but they play a complex game beyond that, taking advantage of the fluid nature of the fae perspective in all it's forms in order to foster distrust in one's self and others and them in you and ideally try to influence a changeling to change their mind on deep, fundamental levels so that even a partial success yields long standing results. But it works because of the premise that we can accept in the comfort of our homes, because we have, for the most part, bought into the books.<br /> <br /> Mage though? Mage doesn't have exterior circumstances like this. This is not a game heavily about the impact of outside influences and how one shifts from one view to another, this is a game about the failures and triumphs of the human will, that change is fundamentally at the hands of the person confronted with it. So we as players, looking in, just see a classic scenario we have seen in media countless times with no real personal experience for why they would say &quot;Sure, I'll join.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, intellectually we know that the stress and the fear and the confusion and the anger and the <i>everything</i> going on at the time might sway us one way or another, but we've also been trained to know the answer is NO in that scenario, that principles are worth dying for and important and generally we've just seen enough shit that portrays saying &quot;I choose death&quot; in a positive light. And from the comfort of our own homes, secure in our knowledge and faith and feelings and bathrobes, it's easy to say &quot;I wouldn't join.&quot; And so when you're trying to convince someone that they might, of course they're going to say no. It's not compelling. It's not an invasive scenario, it doesn't subvert or challenge one's conventional understandings. People <i>know</i> to say No to that. They know to say No to the guy trying to buy you.<br /> <br /> If there is an appeal to make, It is not through blatant displays of force, it's through subtle and insidious manipulations of that which a person takes pride in. The Seers aren't going to put a gun to your head, they're going to find ways to make you question yourself, what you stand for. They will find the cracks in your armor and they will take advantage of that with velvet gloves. Sure, they'll keep up exterior pressure, but they aren't going to compromise the entire's organization as the soft second place.<br /> <br /> If the Seers try to win someone over, the first thing they are always going to do is get someone to <i>give up</i>. Completely on their own accord.<br /> <br /> And, you know, it's hard for anyone to know just <i>how</i> they would give up. The worlds we live in seem very sure to us-they are designed that way, and we are programmed to make it easy to find, because otherwise we'd be gibbering balls of neuroses on overload. These things seem safe and solid to us, and it takes a lot to make them ephemeral. If you told me five years ago that I would be planning on leaving the Mormon Church, I'd have laughed at you. It now seems inevitable to me, but then, it was inconceivable, and that's with me having been aware of a majority of the things that did, in fact, go and play into why I finally got tired of the bullshit.<br /> <br /> And this is half of why my point is <i>you won't know until you're there</i>, because it's inconceivable to see that which is firm around us fade away into smoke. This is why I generally do not posit why Kumiko specifically would. It's a personal affair.<br /> <br /> (The other half of the point is that saying &quot;i wouldn't&quot; basically reads to me as &quot;I'm not examining with myself with a critical eye, looking for weaknesses, and shoring up against them, so by all means go for it&quot;, and further stills that those flaws are perceived as possibly not having a place in the Way Things Are and something that needs to be accepted for one's long term transcendence.)<br /> <br /> And strictly speaking, it's also, from an in-universe perspective, not very practical for the Seers to go around doing the &quot;Gun to Head&quot; conversion trick. You might win a temporary ally, but you have also laid the seeds of future shit-kicking going down. The Seers might be a contentious bunch, fighting each other over positions and such, but they still wouldn't want to essentially hire someone in a way that invites them to set them up the bomb at the worst possible time.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, no, if you want to try and open someone to the possibility of them joining the bad guys, don't go with a classical black and white scene we've all seen and know the answer to. Argue from a position that is chartreuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Seers vary as much as anyone else, so there are definitely those who would go the gun to the head route. That said, I'm talking about those that aren't <i>obviously</i> going with the gun to the head method. Make no mistake, there is totally a gun to your head in this scenario, but it's one that most people aren't going to spot until the triggers been pulled. But Kumiko has stated that she's really good at seeing through such a ruse so I'm throwing her a bone in this situation in saying that you at least suspect that there's a threat of death involved. Again, I'm using the Executive Suite as my example of how a group of Seers might go about this. They'll give you an 'interview' to try to persuade a new mage to join. If said mage rejects their offer, they kill them and dump the body. They don't tell them that's what's going to happen, but instead of just saying doing what you see yourself doing in a neutral setting has straight up gotten you killed, I gave the benefit of the doubt and said she knew, and in knowing, she could now make a more informed decision. Would she join the Seers (if only for a time), risk building up sympathetic links that will make things all the more difficult if and when she ever decides to defect, and potentially expose those she cares for to retaliation, or choose the death anyways knowing how they'll react to her rejection. <br /> <br /> Now honestly, I don't really see most anyone actually choosing death regardless of what they might say online, but I feel that a lot can be gleaned from the answer, which is why I asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:23:08-07:00","id":971491,"title":"","content":"I see the seers as much more subtle than simple death threats with the very scary possibility of you working for them without realizing. And that means even when you think your doign something against them or opposing them in some way you realize (or more often you don't ever realise) that you just did what they wanted you to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:38:58-07:00","id":971792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971370#post971370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that it's not a convincing argument in this situation.<br /> <br /> Let me go to a similar case I used in Changeling for some clarification-A Huntsman grabs a newly returned changeling, drags them to the edge of Arcadia, and gives them a choice: Help us or go back. In this scenario, there's a widely understood and oft-ac