":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:06:57-07:00","id":971799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=971372#post971372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, sure, I'll do that after this.<br /> <br /> And cool, I'm for that. I get that. My point is that that might not always be the case, and that I feel the best way of ensuring it stays that way is to explore all the ways you might not stay in that place and put your guards on that.<br /> <br /> Know Thyself is key to any form of integrity, and it is a very bittersweet thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Don't hate because I know myself and accept it. It took years and I am still learning but I know my core personality. It's caused me huge in IRL and as a real person, a regular person without power. As a mage with actual real power? It isn't even a realistic question. Go ahead and kill me. I know you're lying so bring it on and stop insulting me and my friends. Would be what I said to said Seer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:27:10-07:00","id":971938,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Actually, no, we won't do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-18-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:47:18-07:00","id":972404,"title":"","content":"I feel like this entire argument is premised on the idea that the Seers are giving you the hard sell. Do we think that they do that, though?<br /> <br /> I mean, they recruit people, yes, because they need tools and cannon fodder, but - crucially - they're not rewarded for swelling the ranks as such, but for climbing them, and every new recruit is a potential competitor. And while it's also true that every new Seer recruit is an opportunity stolen from the clutches of the Pentacle, so is a dead mage.<br /> <br /> I think it's entirely possible that if someone isn't immediately receptive to the basic appeal of the Seers - to immediate status and luxury - then that person is just crossed off the list permanently. Why expend a lot of energy trying to change someone's mind about letting you share your power with them? Especially when that early reluctance could be a red flag signaling trouble down the road, when power and experience have made them more formidable?<br /> <br /> In this take, the stops would only really get pulled out if the person had something the Seers specifically wanted, like a unique insight, a special talent, or a promising destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","user":"jacobkosh","date":". 09-19-2016, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T03:32:31-07:00","id":972437,"title":"","content":"I also feel like this points up one of the key differences between the Ladder and the Seers. The former want companions and fellow travelers in Awakening; they want to share it with anyone who can handle it, which is ideally the whole human race. The latter's feelings about Awakening are that &quot;it makes me better than other people/shows that I was better all along,&quot; &quot;good thing it happened to me and not some other, less deserving schlub,&quot; and &quot;the bosses don't want too many of these.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:56:05-07:00","id":976548,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Silver Ladder and any individual sleeper's place on it. The Silver Ladder isn't oriented around assigning anyone to any job or place in society against their will, instead they want to direct society to the point where everyone has the ability to explore themselves to the degree necessary to figure out what they need to do to live a fulfilling life and also have the freedom to pursue whatever that is.<br /> <br /> No one who doesn't like the work should be forced into being an (whatever), those who enjoy being (whatevers) should be able to make a living doing (whatever) that allows them the time and means to pursure enjoyment outside of (whatever)ing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:41:06-07:00","id":976571,"title":"","content":"Also, if we're being real? If someone came to me and told me they could lift me out of poverty in exchange for performing various immoral actions that I could never be punished for by sleeper authorities because I'm a wizard? I'd be very sorely tempted. Poverty <i>sucks</i>, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:11:53-07:00","id":976650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=976571#post976571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if we're being real? If someone came to me and told me they could lift me out of poverty in exchange for performing various immoral actions that I could never be punished for by sleeper authorities because I'm a wizard? I'd be very sorely tempted. Poverty <i>sucks</i>, yo.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the best things is that what they give you are <i>assignments</i>. A lot of times they don't really care <i>how</i> you get it done, just that you're willing to get it done. You're free to delegate specifics of your task to your lessers. So if they give you something you <i>really</i> don't want to do yourself you can pay/bribe/mind control someone else into doing it for you. Don't want to burn down an apartment building yourself? Find a budding arsonist who is already inclined to do it and pay them to do it. I mean chances are they were going to do something like this themselves anyway eventually, right? Just give em' a little push. And if your conscience won't leave you alone about it afterwards you could either magic it quiet or give the cops an anonymous tip leading to the one who did it. Now there's one less person freely willing to commit arson running around in the wild. Right and wrong cancel out at least a little bit, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:56:40-07:00","id":976674,"title":"","content":"Heck, you want to be even more hands-off, use Fate to doom said building and let <i><b>it</b></i> find the budding arsonist and set them to it. One could argue that's merely making sure that the tragedy that was bound to happen, eventually, happens on your target. You might need to double-check Time to be sure you're going to succeed with such an approach, but yeah, that approach would be easy to rationalize for <i>many</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T17:08:47-07:00","id":976811,"title":"","content":"Nah IMO you don't get to weasel word your way out of the moral cost of being a Seer. The Exarchs won't let you, because that's part of your end of the bargain. YOU burned that orphanage down, even if you didn't light the place up yourself. The Evil Shitheel Gods told you to burn down the orphanage and in exchange for your unquestioning obedience they give you magic and wealth and power. I'm fully aware of the fact that I'd find it so much easier to sleep at night after committing those actions if the payment was dragging myself and by extension my family out of poverty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:47:46-07:00","id":976923,"title":"","content":"Oh make no mistake, doing the things we've mentioned in no way makes you any less morally responsible. Not really, anyways. But what it does is give a person an <i>excuse</i>. A <i>justification</i> that they can use to lie to themselves and somewhat separate what they've done. In all actuality if you pay someone to do it or use magic to nudge fate into having it done it is still <i>all your fault</i> it happened, and in the back of your head you know that for a fact, but it gives you just enough reasoning to scrap a lie together to hide behind, so you can convince yourself that you really aren't as bad as you really are.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though keep in mind that I'm almost exclusively talking about non-Prelate Seers. Once you have a direct line to the Exarchs in your mind and soul things get a bit harder to justify/ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T23:09:25-07:00","id":976996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=976923#post976923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh make no mistake, doing the things we've mentioned in no way makes you any less morally responsible. Not really, anyways. But what it does is give a person an <i>excuse</i>. A <i>justification</i> that they can use to lie to themselves and somewhat separate what they've done. In all actuality if you pay someone to do it or use magic to nudge fate into having it done it is still <i>all your fault</i> it happened, and in the back of your head you know that for a fact, but it gives you just enough reasoning to scrap a lie together to hide behind, so you can convince yourself that you really aren't as bad as you really are.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though keep in mind that I'm almost exclusively talking about non-Prelate Seers. Once you have a direct line to the Exarchs in your mind and soul things get a bit harder to justify/ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it would like Wisdom roll bonus or higher Tier altogether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T05:24:03-07:00","id":977129,"title":"","content":"It's probably the kind of thing Seers encourage, as it allows for the lower-ranking Seers to get some experience under their belt as well as show they're less hung up on old-fashioned morality than their superiors, who are then presumably at the wrong end of a countdown of the subordinate's plans to give themself a promotion.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you're too squeamish to do something, and your subordinate isn't, they may be a more ideal candidate for your position, and in showing themselves willing to kill, can just get rid of you and take your spot. It gets some undesirables out of the Seers, promotes the agenda, and sends a message to everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-27-2016, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:32:16-07:00","id":977566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/963522-why-silver-ladder-should-never-fulfill-their-dreams?p=976923#post976923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh make no mistake, doing the things we've mentioned in no way makes you any less morally responsible. Not really, anyways. But what it does is give a person an <i>excuse</i>. A <i>justification</i> that they can use to lie to themselves and somewhat separate what they've done. In all actuality if you pay someone to do it or use magic to nudge fate into having it done it is still <i>all your fault</i> it happened, and in the back of your head you know that for a fact, but it gives you just enough reasoning to scrap a lie together to hide behind, so you can convince yourself that you really aren't as bad as you really are.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though keep in mind that I'm almost exclusively talking about non-Prelate Seers. Once you have a direct line to the Exarchs in your mind and soul things get a bit harder to justify/ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah... this was exactly where <i>I</i> was going with that, too.<br /> <br /> &quot;Easier to justify to yourself&quot; doesn't mean &quot;not evil&quot; by any stretch. <i>Integrity</i> certainly <b>should</b> get a bonus on degradation tests due to indirection. It's simply less stressful if you can't see eyes, etc. when abusing someone. Wisdom, though, is not Integrity. You'd need to monitor the fallout from the spell and so forth. Do <i>that</i> and you can have a high-Wisdom Seer. Given the loss of Integrity, one could argue mages no longer <i>have</i> any such human compunctions of such a sort.<br /> <br /> (Of course, the attempt to divorce Wisdom from morality was incomplete. I'm considering restoring Morality to sit parallel if I can get a group up for a new Aw 2e game. That way, there's less temptation to conflate the concepts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:48:18-07:00","id":977663,"title":"","content":"The AoH given in the book are just examples, you're encouraged to add or drop whatever you want. The list in the book might not be totally divorced from morality, but Wisdom is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}